MX["5.0"]={"code":"06.1","title":"The Rules Investigator","q":"Why do schools need rules? · CASE FILE → LISTEN → VOCAB → GRAMMAR → WORLD RULES → INTERVIEW → VERDICT","end":{"t":"🕵️ CASE CLOSED – RULES INVESTIGATOR","did":"You investigated school rules, used vocabulary about behaviour, practised have to / mustn’t / don’t have to and passive + to-infinitive, interviewed a classmate and gave a verdict on a rule. 🏅 Badge: RULES INVESTIGATOR","r":"I think this rule is … because …"},"steps":[{"i":"🗂️","n":"01 · Rules without rules?","t":"think","x":5,"h":"🗂️ GETTING STARTED. Why do we need rules? Is it possible to have a school without rules?","lab":["🟢 YES","🔴 NO","🟡 MAYBE, WITH LIMITS"],"items":[["Can a school work without rules?",[0,1,2],"position"]],"pr":"Why do you think so? Give at least one reason (safe, respect, learn, freedom…).","bt":"Lock my position","sg":"Locked! Now build a longer answer."},{"i":"💬","n":"Build my answer","t":"book","lbl":"FRAME","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"💬 Use a frame to explain your position.","items":[["🧱","1","Why do we need rules?","I think schools need rules because …",["safe","respect","learn","fair"],"because"],["⚖️","2","What might happen without rules?","In my opinion, a school without rules would …",["chaos","unsafe","noisy","free"],"would"]]},{"i":"🎬","n":"02 · Watch: first impression","t":"mcq","x":4,"tr":"5.0","ctx":"🎬 Thay cho Track 33. Xem video <a href=\"https://www.esl-lab.com/interviews/a-school-rules/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline text-blue-600\">School Rules and Policies</a> (Randall’s ESL Cyber Listening Lab, phỏng vấn Aubrey về nội quy trường học, khoảng 2 phút). Bật phụ đề tiếng Anh nếu cần. Xem lần 1 để nắm ý chính, rồi trả lời.","items":[{"q":"EX 1. What impression do you get of Aubrey’s attitude towards school rules?","o":["She accepts that some rules are reasonable, but thinks others are unfair or too strict.","She thinks a school should have no rules at all.","She thinks every school rule is perfect."],"a":0,"h":"Listen to how she talks about the dress code and the no-food policy.","r":"She accepts some rules but criticises others."}]},{"i":"🔁","n":"Watch again · Questions a–d","t":"book","lbl":"EX 2","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"oc":1,"tr":"5.0","h":"🔁 EX 2 (video thay cho Track 33). Xem lại video, rồi trả lời bằng ý của em, dựa vào những gì Aubrey và Randall thật sự nói.","items":[["📜","a","Give two examples of the rules or policies they discuss. Use: Schools have … / Students aren’t allowed to … / Students are expected to …","Students are expected to … / There is a rule that …",["dress code","no-food policy","bullying","being late"],"dress|cloth|food|eat|bully|late|start"],["💭","b","What are Aubrey’s opinions about school rules and policies?","Aubrey thinks … because …",["unfair","tricky","lenient"],"because|think|feel|unfair|tricky|ridiculous"],["🎤","c","Can you tell what the interviewer’s (Randall’s) opinions are? Do you think he expected Aubrey to answer as she did?","I think Randall … because …",[],".{12,}"],["🙋","d","What do you think about the rules and policies they talk about?","In my opinion, … because …",["because"],"because|think|opinion"]],"sg":"💡 Đối chiếu với video (chi tiết có trong lời thoại): Aubrey nói quy định về trang phục thường nhắm vào nữ sinh (‘a little sexist’), nhưng cũng đồng ý không nên mặc áo có chữ ‘Violence is awesome!’. Cô không thích chính sách cấm ăn trong lớp vì học sinh tuổi teen hay đói, nhưng hiểu lý do (bừa bộn, gọi đồ ăn giao tận lớp là không chấp nhận được). Về bắt nạt: khó vì có thể diễn ra online và nhà trường khó chứng minh. Về đi muộn: trường học bắt đầu lúc 7 giờ sáng là quá sớm vì học sinh cần ngủ nhiều, nên nên linh hoạt. Randall đồng ý nên có một số quy định về trang phục và về loại đồ ăn gây bẩn."},{"i":"📖","n":"03 · Vocabulary file","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Meaning check: school-rules words.","items":[{"q":"If a school is strict, its rules are …","o":["optional","strongly enforced","not very important"],"a":1,"h":"Strict = nghiêm khắc.","r":"strict = strongly enforced"},{"q":"If you break the rules, you …","o":["write them","obey them","do not follow them"],"a":2,"h":"Break = vi phạm.","r":"break the rules = not follow them"},{"q":"Which means “ở lại sau giờ học để bị phạt”?","o":["get a detention","good behaviour","show respect"],"a":0,"h":"Detention.","r":"get a detention"},{"q":"Students who get into trouble …","o":["leave early","are in trouble with a teacher","win a prize"],"a":1,"h":"Trouble = rắc rối.","r":"get into trouble = be blamed or punished"},{"q":"Choose the best word: Students should show ___ to their teachers.","o":["strict","detention","respect"],"a":2,"h":"Noun after show.","r":"show respect"}]},{"i":"🏫","n":"Describe the school","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":20,"h":"🏫 EX 3. Describe the school using the vocabulary box. Base it on the audio.","items":[["🧐","1","How strict is the school?","The school seems quite strict because …",["strict","respect","good behaviour"],"strict|respect|behaviour"],["⚠️","2","What happens if students break the rules?","If students break the rules, they might …",["get into trouble","get a detention","stay behind after school"],"trouble|detention|stay behind"]]},{"i":"🧪","n":"04 · Grammar lab","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Formula: Subject + be + past participle + to + verb.","items":[{"q":"Students are expected ___ their teachers politely.","o":["to answer","answer","answering"],"a":0,"h":"to + verb.","r":"are expected to answer"},{"q":"We aren’t ___ to wear earphones.","o":["allow","allowed","allowing"],"a":1,"h":"Passive: past participle.","r":"aren’t allowed to"},{"q":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["Students are encouraged work in groups.","Students encouraged to work in groups.","Students are encouraged to work in groups."],"a":2,"h":"be + V3 + to.","r":"are encouraged to work"},{"q":"Are you ___ to know all the rules?","o":["supposed","supposing","suppose"],"a":0,"h":"Passive again.","r":"Are you supposed to…?"}]},{"i":"🚦","n":"have to · mustn’t · don’t have to","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Choose the best meaning.","items":[{"q":"They ___ wear the correct school uniform. (It is required.)","o":["don’t have to","have to","mustn’t"],"a":1,"h":"Required = have to.","r":"have to"},{"q":"Students ___ talk in the corridors. (It is forbidden.)","o":["have to","don’t have to","mustn’t"],"a":2,"h":"Forbidden = mustn’t.","r":"mustn’t"},{"q":"You ___ have lunch in the canteen. (It is not necessary.)","o":["don’t have to","mustn’t","have to"],"a":0,"h":"Not necessary.","r":"don’t have to"},{"q":"“You don’t have to bring lunch” means …","o":["You are not allowed to bring lunch.","You can bring lunch if you want.","You must bring lunch."],"a":1,"h":"Not the same as mustn’t.","r":"Bringing lunch is not compulsory."}]},{"i":"🌍","n":"05 · World rules challenge","t":"mcq","x":5,"ctx":"EX 4. Choose the correct form of the verb in brackets.","items":[{"q":"In Japan, school children (expect) ___ to help to clean and tidy the classrooms at the end of the day.","o":["expect","are expecting","are expected"],"a":2,"h":"Passive.","r":"are expected"},{"q":"Schools in France (not / allow) ___ to serve tomato ketchup.","o":["aren’t allowed","don’t allow","not allowed"],"a":0,"h":"be + not + V3.","r":"aren’t allowed"},{"q":"At some primary schools in the UK, every student (encourage) ___ to run a mile before lessons.","o":["encourages","is encouraged","are encouraged"],"a":1,"h":"Every student = singular.","r":"is encouraged"},{"q":"In China, students (expect) ___ to have a nap at midday.","o":["are expect","expected","are expected"],"a":2,"h":"Plural subject.","r":"are expected"}]},{"i":"🧱","n":"Rule builder","t":"book","lbl":"EX 5","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🧱 EX 5. Complete the rules of the school you heard. Phrases: answer teachers politely · chat to each other in class · talk to visitors · have a mobile out in class · interrupt when someone is speaking · look out of the window · sit up straight in class · talk in the corridors. Check with the audio.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Make a rule with “expected to”.","They’re expected to …",["answer teachers politely","sit up straight in class","talk to visitors"],"expected to"],["2️⃣","2","Make a rule with “not allowed to”.","They’re not allowed to …",["have a mobile out in class","chat to each other in class","talk in the corridors"],"allowed to"],["3️⃣","3","Make a rule with “supposed to” or “encouraged to”.","They’re supposed to … / They’re encouraged to …",["interrupt when someone is speaking","look out of the window"],"supposed to|encouraged to"]]},{"i":"🎙️","n":"06 · Interview planner","t":"book","lbl":"PLAN","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🎙️ EX 6. In groups of three: interviewer + two students. Start: “Tell me, what’s it like to be a student at this school? Are there a lot of rules? Can you give me some examples?”","items":[["📜","1","Rule 1: What do students have to do?","Well, students have to …",["Well …","For one thing …"],"have to|expected to"],["🚫","2","Rule 2: What aren’t students allowed to do?","Another rule is that students aren’t allowed to …",["Another rule is that …"],"allowed to|mustn"],["⚖️","3","Your opinion: are these rules fair?","I think these rules are … because …",[],"because"]]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"Natural responses","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Useful expressions from the book.","items":[{"q":"Which phrase introduces a new idea?","o":["Another rule is that …","I see","That’s right …"],"a":0,"h":"Introduce an idea.","r":"Another rule is that …"},{"q":"Which phrase shows surprise?","o":["Well …","Oh, I see …","For one thing …"],"a":1,"h":"Oh, right / Oh, I see.","r":"Oh, I see …"}]},{"i":"⚖️","n":"07 · Group discussion","t":"book","lbl":"EX 7","sv":"Save","x":3,"min":10,"h":"⚖️ EX 7. Discuss in groups, then note your own ideas.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Are rules important at school? Why?","Rules are important because …",[],""],["2️⃣","2","Which rules are most helpful?","The most helpful rule is … because …",[],""],["3️⃣","3","What leads to good behaviour? Is it only rules?","Good behaviour also comes from …",[],""],["4️⃣","4","Who should make the rules?","The rules should be made by …",[],""],["5️⃣","5","Is it ever right to break the rules?","It might be right to break a rule when …",[],""]]},{"i":"🚦","n":"Rule sorter","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"🚦 SORT THE RULES. Is each rule compulsory, forbidden or not necessary?","hint":"have to = must do · mustn’t = not allowed · don’t have to = not necessary, you can choose.","lab":["✅ HAVE TO","⛔ MUSTN’T","🟡 DON’T HAVE TO"],"items":[["Students ___ wear the correct school uniform.",0],["Students ___ shout or run in the corridors.",1],["Students ___ wear earphones in school.",1],["If they are absent, students ___ bring a note from their parents.",0],["Students ___ have lunch in the school canteen (they can bring their own).",2],["Students ___ serve the food and drinks for each other at lunch.",0],["Students ___ talk in the corridors.",1]],"sg":"💡 Remember: don’t have to is NOT the same as mustn’t."},{"i":"🎙️","n":"Build the interview","t":"order","x":12,"items":[0],"h":"🎙️ Put the interview in order: the interviewer’s three questions, then the student’s answers.","hint":"Questions first, then answers. Use the speaking tip: Well … For one thing … Another rule is that …","cards":["A. Tell me, what’s it like to be a student at this school?","B. Well … there are quite a lot of rules.","C. Can you give me some examples?","D. Another rule is that we mustn’t talk in the corridors.","E. Are there a lot of rules?","F. For one thing, we have to wear the correct uniform."],"ans":[0,4,2,1,5,3],"yl":"🎙️ YOUR INTERVIEW","ft":"🎙️ INTERVIEW READY","flow":["QUESTION 1","QUESTION 2","QUESTION 3","START THE ANSWER","FIRST RULE","ANOTHER RULE"],"bm":"Not quite. The interviewer asks three questions first; then the student answers: Well … For one thing … Another rule is that …"},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Fair or unfair?","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 YOUR RULE. YOUR VERDICT. Choose one school rule. Is it fair and necessary, unfair or too strict, or does it depend? Give a reason or example and say what you would change.","hint":"The rule is … It is fair / unfair / depends because … For example, … I would change … / Students should …","ph":"One rule at my school is that students are expected to … I think it is … because … For example, … I would change …","checks":[["Identifies a school rule","rule|allowed|expected|supposed|encouraged|have to|mustn",1],["Gives a clear opinion","fair|unfair|strict|necessary|depends|i think|in my opinion",1],["Gives a reason or example","because|for example|for instance|so that",1],["Uses target grammar","(allowed|expected|encouraged|supposed) to|have to|mustn.t|don.t have to",1],["Suggests an improvement","would change|should|could|instead|rather",1]],"sk":["I can understand an interview about school rules.","I can use vocabulary about rules and behaviour.","I can distinguish have to, mustn’t and don’t have to.","I can use be allowed / expected / encouraged / supposed to + verb.","I can ask and answer questions about school rules.","I can explain whether a rule is fair and why."]}],"mx":208};
MX["5.1"]={"code":"06.2","title":"The Kaizen Coach","q":"What can families learn from the way businesses work? · FAMILY → READ → VOCAB → CASE FILE → PASSIVE INFINITIVE → KAIZEN → BETTER SYSTEM","end":{"t":"🏅 MISSION COMPLETE – KAIZEN COACH","did":"You explored family life, read about a Swedish family and kaizen, used home and business vocabulary, practised the passive infinitive, evaluated a method and designed a small improvement plan. 🏅 Badge: KAIZEN COACH","r":"A small change I can make is … and I will review it by …"},"steps":[{"i":"🏠","n":"01 · Family life","t":"book","lbl":"WARM-UP","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🏠 GETTING STARTED. What are the best things about family life?","items":[["💛","1","What is the best thing about family life?","One of the best things about family life is …",["support","belong","share","learn"],""],["😵","2","What can make family life difficult?","Family life can become stressful when …",["chores","busy","disagree","no routine"],""]]},{"i":"🔮","n":"02 · Predict","t":"think","x":3,"h":"🔮 BEFORE READING. The title is “Run your home like a business”. What do you think the family changed?","lab":["🧩 ROUTINES & RESPONSIBILITIES","💰 STARTED A BUSINESS","📏 STRICTER RULES","✈️ MORE HOLIDAYS"],"items":[["What did the family change?",[0,1,2,3],"prediction"]],"pr":"Why do you think so? You will check while reading.","bt":"Lock my prediction","sg":"Locked! Read the article (Ex 1) and test it."},{"i":"📰","n":"Main idea","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1","sv":"Save","x":8,"min":25,"h":"📰 EX 1. Read the article. How did a business idea help family life? Write your answer with your own words.","items":[["🎯","1","How did a business idea help family life?","The family used … to improve … They made changes to …, which helped them …",["kaizen","routines","happier","less stressful"],"kaizen|business|method|approach"]]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Evidence hunt","t":"book","lbl":"STAGE","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🔎 Find evidence in the article for each stage. Do not guess from the title.","items":[["⚠️","A. Problem","What was life like before? (clues: hectic, chaos, stressed)","Before, the family …",["hectic","chaos","stressed"],""],["🛠️","B. Method","What method did they use and why? (clues: kaizen, strategy, efficiency)","They chose … because …",["kaizen","strategy","efficiency"],""],["🌈","C. Result","What was the result? (clues: improvements, routines, happier, relaxed)","After the changes, they felt …",["happier","relaxed","improvements"],""]]},{"i":"📖","n":"03 · Vocabulary file","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 2. Match the meaning.","items":[{"q":"A very busy and active schedule","o":["efficiency","resentment","hectic"],"a":2,"h":"Busy, rushed.","r":"hectic"},{"q":"Washing, cleaning and ironing at home","o":["household chores","executive","workload"],"a":0,"h":"Jobs at home.","r":"household chores"},{"q":"A plan or approach to reach a goal","o":["employee","strategy","resentment"],"a":1,"h":"Plan.","r":"strategy"},{"q":"To help and share the work","o":["process","set goals","pitch in"],"a":2,"h":"Phrasal verb.","r":"pitch in"},{"q":"A feeling of anger because something seems unfair","o":["resentment","schedule","productivity"],"a":0,"h":"Bitter feeling.","r":"resentment"},{"q":"The amount of work a person has to do","o":["system","workload","management"],"a":1,"h":"Business studies.","r":"workload"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Use the words","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Word bank: pitch in · schedule · household chores · hectic · process","items":[{"q":"When everyone is busy, family life can become ___.","o":["schedule","process","hectic"],"a":2,"h":"Busy and rushed.","r":"hectic"},{"q":"Washing, cleaning and ironing are examples of ___.","o":["household chores","hectic","pitch in"],"a":0,"h":"Jobs at home.","r":"household chores"},{"q":"A clear ___ can help people organise their time.","o":["pitch in","schedule","process"],"a":1,"h":"Time plan.","r":"schedule"},{"q":"When family members ___, they share the work.","o":["schedule","hectic","pitch in"],"a":2,"h":"Help together.","r":"pitch in"},{"q":"Setting goals and reviewing a ___ can help people improve a system.","o":["process","hectic","household chores"],"a":0,"h":"Steps of work.","r":"process"}]},{"i":"✅","n":"Check with the article","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Facts from “Run your home like a business” (pages 124–125). Use them to check your Ex 3 answers.","items":[{"q":"Why did the family need to change?","o":["They had lost their jobs.","Their life had become hectic, the house was in chaos and everyone was stressed.","They wanted to move to a new house."],"a":1,"h":"First paragraph.","r":"Hectic life, chaos at home, stress."},{"q":"Why did they choose kaizen, a business method?","o":["A friend told them about it.","It was a school rule.","Eva had seen it improve productivity and efficiency at a pharmaceutical company, and Mattias had seen it work smoothly in hospitals."],"a":2,"h":"Both parents knew it from work.","r":"Eva and Mattias knew kaizen from their jobs."},{"q":"What did the new house rules say about laundry?","o":["Whoever filled a laundry bag had to load the washing machine, then the clothes were dried and ironed.","Only the parents could do the laundry.","Laundry was done once a month."],"a":0,"h":"Four colour bags.","r":"Whoever filled the bag loaded the machine."},{"q":"What happens at the weekly family meeting?","o":["They choose who wins a prize.","On Sunday evenings, in 15 minutes, they discuss the coming fortnight, set goals and decide how to solve problems.","They watch a film."],"a":1,"h":"Two-week schedule.","r":"15-minute Sunday meeting about the next two weeks."},{"q":"In the article, what are the ‘knots’?","o":["Decorations in the house","Shoes by the door","The problems that were slowing things down"],"a":2,"h":"Process = thread.","r":"The problems slowing things down."}]},{"i":"🗃️","n":"04 · Reading case file","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🗃️ EX 3. Answer one question at a time using the article. For E–G, explain your reasoning.","items":[["A","a","Why did the Swedish family decide they needed to make changes in their home life?","They decided … because …",["hectic","chaos","stress"],""],["B","b","Why did they choose a business method to help them make the changes?","They chose it because … (think about Eva and Mattias’s experience)",[],""],["C","c","What kind of new rules did the family make? (check the article)","They made rules about …",[],""],["D","d","Why did they start having a family meeting once a week?","They started it so that …",[],""],["E","e","Why do you think making schedules and setting goals were necessary?","I think … because …",["schedule","set goals","responsibilities"],"because"],["F","f","Has the process been a success? How do you know?","I think it has / hasn’t been a success because the article says …",["happier","relaxed"],"because|says|article"],["G","g","Can you think of any disadvantages of the process?","One possible disadvantage is …",["too strict","less free"],"disadvantage|might|could"]]},{"i":"🧪","n":"05 · Passive infinitive","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Language tip: passive infinitive = to be + past participle (V3). “…with piles of washing to be done and clothes to be ironed.”","items":[{"q":"Which is the passive infinitive of “to iron the clothes”?","o":["to be ironed","to be iron","to ironing"],"a":0,"h":"to be + V3.","r":"to be ironed"},{"q":"There are many dishes ___ after dinner.","o":["being wash","to be washed","to wash"],"a":1,"h":"Dishes receive the action.","r":"to be washed"},{"q":"These clothes need ___.","o":["ironing be","to iron","to be ironed"],"a":2,"h":"Need + passive infinitive.","r":"need to be ironed"},{"q":"The tasks have ___ before the weekend.","o":["to be completed","completing","to complete"],"a":0,"h":"Tasks are completed.","r":"have to be completed"}]},{"i":"🧹","n":"Your sentence","t":"book","lbl":"TASK","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"h":"🧹 Choose a task (the washing · the dishes · the rooms · the shopping) and write one sentence with to be + past participle.","items":[["✏️","1","Complete: There is / are … to be …","There is a lot of washing to be done.",["the washing","the dishes","the rooms","the shopping"],"to be [a-z]+"]]},{"i":"💡","n":"06 · Kaizen think tank","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Kaizen is a Japanese word meaning improvement. It is used in business and management to improve productivity, efficiency and processes.","items":[{"q":"Kaizen means …","o":["competition","improvement","punishment"],"a":1,"h":"Japanese word.","r":"improvement"},{"q":"Why can kaizen improve productivity and efficiency?","o":["It removes the need to plan or review work.","It means people must work faster all the time.","It helps people find and improve inefficient routines."],"a":2,"h":"Small steps, regular review.","r":"It helps people improve routines step by step."}]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"Speaking Ex 4","t":"book","lbl":"EX 4","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":20,"h":"🗣️ EX 4. Discuss, then write your ideas. Explain your reasoning.","items":[["A","a","Why do you think this method is used to improve productivity and efficiency?","I think this method improves efficiency because …",[],"because"],["B","b","Does it need to be a continuous process? Why?","In my opinion, improvement should be continuous because …",[],"because"],["C","c","Is it only managers and executives, or other workers too? Is that important? Why?","I believe employees should be involved because …",["employees","managers"],"because"]]},{"i":"🛠️","n":"Improvement plan","t":"book","lbl":"PLAN","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🛠️ DESIGN A BETTER SYSTEM (web extension). Pick a problem: chores not shared fairly · forgotten homework deadlines · little family time · disorganised routines.","items":[["⚠️","1","Identify the problem","The problem is that …",["chores","deadlines","family time","routines"],""],["🔧","2","Propose one small change","One small change is … / We could …",[],""],["🎯","3","Set a goal","Our goal is to …",["set goals"],"goal"],["📊","4","How will you review the result?","We will review it by … / every week …",["weekly meeting","check"],"review|check|meeting|every"]]},{"i":"📰","n":"The kaizen story","t":"order","x":14,"items":[0],"h":"📰 Put the events of the article in the order they happen.","hint":"Start with the problem, end with the result.","cards":["A. Their home life became happier and more relaxed.","B. They thought of their home as a thread and looked for the ‘knots’.","C. They sorted their dirty clothes into four bags.","D. The family decided to use a business strategy: kaizen.","E. On Sunday evenings they have a 15-minute family meeting.","F. They wrote a two-week schedule and put it on the noticeboard.","G. Life at home became hectic and everyone felt stressed."],"ans":[6,3,1,2,5,4,0],"yl":"📰 YOUR STORY ORDER","ft":"📰 STORY ORDER SET","flow":["PROBLEM","STRATEGY","FIND THE KNOTS","NEW RULE","SHARED PLAN","WEEKLY MEETING","RESULT"],"bm":"Not quite. Think: problem → strategy → changes → result. Check the article."},{"i":"🏢","n":"Business or home?","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"🏢🏠 Sort the words: do they belong to business studies or to family life?","hint":"Look at the Key words box and at the family in the article.","lab":["🏢 BUSINESS WORDS","🏠 FAMILY LIFE WORDS"],"items":[["laundry",1],["noticeboard",1],["household chores",1],["management practice",0],["efficiency",0],["dishwasher",1],["employee",0],["family meeting",1],["executive",0],["productivity",0]],"sg":"💡 Kaizen shows that the same ideas can work in both places."},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Better system","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Write your improvement plan in 4–6 sentences: the problem, one small change, a goal and how you will review the result.","hint":"The problem is … One small change is … Our goal is … We will review it by … This should help because …","ph":"The problem is that … One small change is … Our goal is to … We will review it every week by …","checks":[["Identifies a clear problem","problem|difficult|stress|not shared|forget|disorgani[sz]ed|little time",1],["Suggests a realistic improvement","change|could|should|we will|plan|improve",1],["Sets a clear goal","goal|aim|so that|want to",1],["Explains how to review","review|check|meeting|every|each|weekly",1],["Clear English (a full paragraph)",".{80,}",1]],"sk":["I can explain the main idea of the article about the Swedish family.","I understand vocabulary about household chores and business management.","I can answer reading questions using evidence from the article.","I can recognise and use the passive infinitive.","I can explain the basic idea of kaizen.","I can suggest a practical improvement and explain how to review it."]}],"mx":237};
MX["5.2"]={"code":"06.3","title":"The Family Rules Reporter","q":"Discover the rules. Report the conversation. · WARM-UP → VOCAB → LISTEN → REPORTED SPEECH → ROLE-PLAY → FINAL BOSS","end":{"t":"🎙️ MISSION COMPLETE – FAMILY RULES REPORTER","did":"You talked about home rules, learned five expressions, listened for rules and permission, practised reported questions and statements, role-played a conversation and reported it. 🏅 Badge: FAMILY RULES REPORTER","r":"At home I have to … and I asked if …"},"steps":[{"i":"🏠","n":"01 · Do families need rules?","t":"think","x":4,"h":"🏠 GETTING STARTED. Do families need rules? Why?","lab":["🟢 YES, THEY HELP","🟡 SOME, BUT FLEXIBLE","🔴 TOO MANY = STRESS"],"items":[["Choose your opinion.",[0,1,2],"opinion"]],"pr":"Finish: I think families need / don’t need rules because …","bt":"Lock my opinion","sg":"Locked! Now talk about your own home."},{"i":"🗣️","n":"Home rules","t":"book","lbl":"RULE","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":12,"h":"🗣️ What kind of things do you have rules about at home?","items":[["📱","1","What rules do you have about phones?","At home, I have to … / I’m not allowed to …",["have to","not allowed to"],""],["📚","2","Do you have to do your homework before watching TV?","I have to … / I don’t have to …",[],"have to|allowed"],["🚪","3","Do you have to ask permission before going out?","I have to ask permission before …",["ask permission"],"permission"]]},{"i":"📖","n":"02 · Vocabulary detective","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 2. Five expressions about family rules.","items":[{"q":"a phone-free zone","o":["A place where phones are not allowed","A time for using social media","A place where everyone must use a phone"],"a":0,"h":"Free of phones.","r":"a place where phones are not allowed"},{"q":"a ban on phones at the table","o":["A prize for using phones","An official rule that says you must not do it","A rule that says you must do it"],"a":1,"h":"Ban = cấm.","r":"a ban = it is not allowed"},{"q":"screen time","o":["time for a break from school","time for cleaning screens","time spent using screens"],"a":2,"h":"Time on devices.","r":"time spent using screens"},{"q":"make your bed","o":["tidy and arrange your bed","buy a new bed","sleep early"],"a":0,"h":"Household job.","r":"tidy your bed"},{"q":"ask permission","o":["refuse a request","ask if you are allowed to do something","tell someone what you did"],"a":1,"h":"Ask first.","r":"ask if you are allowed to do something"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Use the expressions","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Extra practice (not from the book).","items":[{"q":"At dinner, we have a ___ on phones.","o":["permission","screen time","ban"],"a":2,"h":"A rule that forbids.","r":"ban"},{"q":"I usually ___ before I leave for school.","o":["make my bed","ask permission","a phone-free zone"],"a":0,"h":"Household chore.","r":"make my bed"},{"q":"My parents limit my ___ to one hour a day.","o":["bed","screen time","ban"],"a":1,"h":"Time on screens.","r":"screen time"},{"q":"I have to ___ before I invite a friend over.","o":["screen time","make my bed","ask permission"],"a":2,"h":"Ask first.","r":"ask permission"}]},{"i":"🎬","n":"03 · Watch: house rules","t":"mcq","x":3,"tr":"5.2","ctx":"🎬 Thay cho Track 34. Xem video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GEXa_WcZZow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline text-blue-600\">My House Rules | Real English Conversation (B1)</a> (Natural English Podcast, B1). Video dài khoảng 45–50 phút, em chỉ cần đoạn nói về quy tắc trong nhà (Useful Phrases, khoảng 4:00–10:00). Bật phụ đề tiếng Anh nếu cần. What rules do the hosts talk about?","items":[{"q":"EX 1. What are the hosts mainly talking about in this part?","o":["Simple household rules: what people can and can’t do at home.","How to cook dinner for a big family.","How to repair things in a house."],"a":0,"h":"Listen to the opening lines.","r":"Simple household rules"},{"q":"EX 3a. What is the rule about shoes?","o":["Everyone must keep shoes on at all times.","Everyone takes off their shoes at the door and doesn’t walk in with muddy shoes.","Shoes are allowed anywhere in the house."],"a":1,"h":"In our house, we take off our shoes at the door.","r":"Take off shoes at the door; no muddy shoes on the carpet"},{"q":"EX 3a. What are the rules about lights and noise?","o":["There are no rules about lights or noise.","Lights must be on all night; music is allowed at any time.","Don’t leave the lights on, and don’t play loud music after 10."],"a":2,"h":"We don’t leave the lights on…","r":"Don’t leave lights on; no loud music after 10"},{"q":"EX 3a. What are the rules about food and meals?","o":["They eat dinner together and don’t eat in the bedroom.","They never eat at home.","Everyone eats alone in their bedroom."],"a":0,"h":"In our house, we eat dinner together.","r":"Eat dinner together; don’t eat in the bedroom"},{"q":"EX 3b. Which phrase is used to say that something is NOT permitted by a rule?","o":["In our house, we eat dinner together.","We are not allowed to …","You can sit anywhere."],"a":1,"h":"Look for ‘not allowed to’.","r":"We are not allowed to …"}]},{"i":"🔁","n":"Compare with your home","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3b / 4","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"oc":1,"tr":"5.2","h":"🔁 EX 3b và 4. Dùng các mẫu câu trong video (In our house, we … / We don’t … / You can … / You can’t … / We are not allowed to … / Please don’t …) để so sánh quy tắc nhà em với quy tắc trong video.","items":[["📜","1","Which rules in the video are the same in your home?","In my house, we … The same rule at my home is …",["In our house, we","We don’t","You can’t"],"in (our|my) house|we|you can"],["⚠️","2","Which rules are different? What are you not allowed to do?","In my house, we are not allowed to …",["We are not allowed to","Please don’t"],"allowed|don.t|can.t|have to"],["🙋","3","What do you have to ask permission for at home?","I have to ask permission to … / We have to …",["ask permission","have to"],"permission|have to|ask"]]},{"i":"🎬","n":"Watch: asking permission","t":"mcq","x":3,"tr":"5.2","ctx":"🎬 Thay cho Track 35. Xem video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8OWTlHI-lo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline text-blue-600\">Teenager Asking Parents for Permission? Say This Instead (English Pod)</a> (English Pod, khoảng 16 phút). Em chỉ cần đoạn hội thoại đầu và phần giải thích cách xin phép lịch sự (khoảng 0:00–4:00). Bật phụ đề tiếng Anh nếu cần. What is the teenager asking permission to do?","items":[{"q":"EX 5. What does the teenager want to do first?","o":["Stay out late with friends.","Get a new phone.","Borrow the car to go to a concert tonight."],"a":2,"h":"Do you think I could borrow the car?","r":"Borrow the car to go to a concert tonight"},{"q":"Why does the dad say no to the car?","o":["He needs the car tonight to pick up the mother.","He doesn’t like concerts.","The car is broken."],"a":0,"h":"He needs it to pick up your mother.","r":"He needs it to pick up the mother"},{"q":"Who asked the teenager to go to the concert?","o":["Her mother.","A boy called Eric asked if she would go with him.","Her best friend Sarah."],"a":1,"h":"Eric asked if I would go with him.","r":"Eric asked if she would go with him"},{"q":"What does the teenager ask for next?","o":["Could I stay up late?","Can I go to bed early?","Would you mind giving me 100 bucks?"],"a":2,"h":"The dad answers ‘No way’.","r":"100 bucks"},{"q":"Which are the polite ways to ask for something in this video?","o":["I was wondering … / Do you think I could … / Would you mind …","Give me … / I want … / Do it now.","Never … / Always … / Maybe …"],"a":0,"h":"Listen after the dialogue.","r":"I was wondering…, Do you think I could…, Would you mind…"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Report the request","t":"book","lbl":"EX 5","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"oc":1,"tr":"5.2","h":"✍️ EX 5. Viết bằng ý của em: nhân vật xin phép làm gì và bố trả lời thế nào? Dùng: The teenager is asking permission to … / She asked if she could … / Her dad told her that …","items":[["👧","1","What is the teenager asking permission to do?","The teenager is asking permission to … / She asked if she could …",["asking permission to","asked if she could"],"asking permission to|asked (if|whether)"],["👨","2","What does her dad say? Report it.","Her dad said (that) … / He told her …",["said","told her"],"said|told"]]},{"i":"🧪","n":"04 · Reported speech rules","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Yes/No: asked if / whether. Wh-: statement word order. Statements: said. Instructions: told + person + to.","items":[{"q":"“Can I stay up late?” →","o":["Alisha said if she can stay up late.","Alisha asked if she could stay up late.","Alisha asked could she stay up late."],"a":1,"h":"if + statement order.","r":"asked if she could"},{"q":"“Whose house are you going to?” →","o":["…asked Raheem if whose house he was going to.","…asked Raheem whose house was he going to.","…asked Raheem whose house he was going to."],"a":2,"h":"Keep wh-word, use statement order.","r":"whose house he was going to"},{"q":"“I want to watch the football match.” →","o":["Alisha said she wanted to watch the football match.","Alisha told she wanted to watch the football match.","Alisha said me she wanted to watch…"],"a":0,"h":"said + clause.","r":"Alisha said she wanted…"},{"q":"“Bring them back.” →","o":["Raheem’s dad told to bring them back.","Raheem’s dad told him to bring them back.","Raheem’s dad said him to bring them back."],"a":1,"h":"told + person + to.","r":"told him to bring them back"}]},{"i":"🎯","n":"Exercise 6 · Choose the report","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 6 (page 127). Choose the correct options to report the questions and statements.","items":[{"q":"a. Alisha to her mum: ‘Can I make a pizza?’ → Alisha ___ if she ___ make a pizza.","o":["asked / can","said / can","asked / could"],"a":2,"h":"Yes/No question: asked if + could.","r":"asked / could"},{"q":"b. Raheem to his dad: ‘We’re going to play table tennis.’ → Raheem ___ they ___ going to play table tennis.","o":["said / were","told / are","said / are"],"a":0,"h":"Statement: said + past form.","r":"said / were"},{"q":"c. Raheem to his dad: ‘Can I take the new balls to play with?’ → Raheem ___ if he ___ take the new balls to play with.","o":["asked / can","asked / could","said / can"],"a":1,"h":"Yes/No question.","r":"asked / could"},{"q":"d. Raheem’s dad to Raheem: ‘Bring them back.’ → Raheem’s dad ___ him to bring them back.","o":["told","said"],"a":0,"h":"tell + person + to.","r":"told"},{"q":"e. Raheem’s dad to Raheem: ‘What time are you going?’ → Raheem’s dad ___ him what time ___ going.","o":["asked / he was","told / he was","asked / was he"],"a":0,"h":"Wh-question: statement word order.","r":"asked / he was"}]},{"i":"🔧","n":"Repair the report","t":"book","lbl":"FIX","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🔧 Fix the reports. Say the correct sentence, then write it.","items":[["❓","1","Direct: “Are you tired?”  Wrong: She asked was I tired.","She asked if / whether I …",["if","whether"],"asked (if|whether) .*was"],["🏠","2","Direct: “Where do you live?”  Wrong: He asked me where did I live.","He asked me where I …",[],"where i lived"],["🚪","3","Direct: “Close the door.”  Wrong: She said me to close the door.","She told me to …",["told"],"told me to close"]]},{"i":"🎭","n":"05 · Role-play & my rules","t":"book","lbl":"SAY","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🎭 EX 4 and 7. Compare family rules with a partner, then role-play in three: teenager, parent, reporter (beach on Sunday · new trainers · friend’s house to watch a film).","items":[["🧑","Teenager","Ask for permission and give a reason.","Can I … ? / Could I … ?",["Can I","Could I"],"can i|could i"],["👨‍👩‍👧","Parent","Ask one follow-up question, then agree or refuse.","Who / What time … ? / You can … if …",["Who","What time"],""],["📝","Reporter","Report the question and the response.","She asked if … / He told her to …",["asked if","told"],"asked|told"],["🏡","My rule","Direct speech → reported speech: My mum says, “…” / My mum says that …","My mum says that I have to …",[],"says|said|told"]]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"Say, tell or ask?","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"🗣️ Which reporting verb completes each report: said, told or asked?","hint":"told is followed by a person (told her); said is not; asked is for questions.","lab":["🗣️ SAID","📣 TOLD + person","❓ ASKED"],"items":[["Alisha ___ she wanted to watch the football match.",0],["Raheem’s dad ___ him to bring them back.",1],["Alisha ___ if she could stay up late.",2],["Raheem ___ they were going to play table tennis.",0],["Alisha’s mum ___ her that she would have to do her homework first.",1],["Raheem’s dad ___ Raheem whose house he was going to.",2]],"sg":"💡 Never say “said me”: use told me, or said."},{"i":"🧱","n":"Build the reported question","t":"order","x":8,"items":[0],"h":"🧱 Put the pieces in order to build the reported question.","hint":"Wh-word, then subject + verb (statement order).","cards":["A. on Saturday.","B. Raheem’s dad","C. he was going to","D. asked Raheem","E. whose house"],"ans":[1,3,4,2,0],"yl":"🧱 YOUR SENTENCE","ft":"🧱 SENTENCE BUILT","flow":["WHO","REPORTING VERB","QUESTION WORD + NOUN","SUBJECT + VERB","TIME"],"bm":"Not quite. Reported questions keep the question word but use statement order: whose house he was going to."},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Family rules reporter","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 A teenager wants to stay at a friend’s house to watch a film. Record the conversation (teenager asks, parent asks, parent responds). Then report it to another family member.","hint":"Teenager: “Can I …?” Parent: “Whose house …?” / “You can … if …” → Report: She asked if … She asked whose house … Her mum told her to …","ph":"Teenager: “Can I stay at Mai’s house?” Parent: “Where does she live?” Report: She asked if … Her mum asked where …","checks":[["Understands the situation (friend’s house / film)","friend|film|house|stay|watch",1],["Reports a yes/no question (asked if / whether)","asked (if|whether)",1],["Uses wh-question word order","asked .*(what|where|who|whose|when|why|how) (i|you|he|she|they|we|it|the)\\b",1],["Reports the response / instruction","told .* to |said (that )?(she|he|they|i)",1],["Completes the task (full report)",".{100,}",1]],"sk":["I can explain the five expressions about family rules.","I can identify rules and requests for permission in the listening.","I can report yes/no questions using if or whether.","I can report wh-questions using statement word order.","I can use said, asked and told correctly in context."]}],"mx":208};
MX["5.3"]={"code":"06.4","title":"The Moral Dilemma Solver","q":"Make a difficult choice. Explain what you would have done. · DILEMMA → READ → THIRD CONDITIONAL → LISTEN → SPEAK","end":{"t":"⚖️ MISSION COMPLETE – MORAL DILEMMA SOLVER","did":"You explained moral dilemmas, read three difficult choices, practised the third conditional and if only, listened to other opinions and justified your own decisions. 🏅 Badge: MORAL DILEMMA SOLVER","r":"If I had …, I would have …"},"steps":[{"i":"⚖️","n":"01 · What is a moral dilemma?","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"A friend says they are being bullied and asks you to keep it secret. You worry it could get worse if no adult knows.","items":[{"q":"What makes this situation difficult?","o":["There is only one obvious choice.","You want to respect your friend’s trust but also protect them.","You must choose a school subject."],"a":1,"h":"Two things matter at once.","r":"Trust and protection conflict."}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Say it","t":"book","lbl":"DEFINE","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"✍️ Finish the sentence in your own words.","items":[["💭","1","Why is it a moral dilemma?","This is a moral dilemma because …",["right","wrong","trust","responsibility"],"because"]]},{"i":"📖","n":"02 · Reading: attitudes","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 1. Read the three posts in your book (Brandon: lost money · Rona: a friend’s secret · Bella: the café bill). Options are suggestions, not an official key.","items":[{"q":"Brandon’s attitude is …","o":["angry with the school","certain he made the perfect decision","uncertain and reflective about what he should have done"],"a":2,"h":"He wonders what he should have done.","r":"uncertain and reflective"},{"q":"Rona’s attitude is …","o":["full of regret","proud and relaxed","bored"],"a":0,"h":"Think about “If only…”.","r":"regretful"},{"q":"Bella’s attitude is …","o":["angry with her bus driver","worried about the waitress","not interested"],"a":1,"h":"Check the text.","r":"worried"}]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Evidence hunt","t":"book","lbl":"EVIDENCE","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🔎 Go back to the book and find evidence for each answer.","items":[["💰","Brandon","What did he do with the money, and why?","He … because …",[],"because"],["🤐","Rona","Why did her friend ask her not to tell anyone?","Her friend asked her not to tell because …",[],""],["☕","Bella","Why didn’t she return to the café immediately?","She didn’t go back because …",[],"because|so"]]},{"i":"✅","n":"Check with the posts","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Facts from the three posts (page 128). Use them to check your answers.","items":[{"q":"Brandon: what did he do with the money?","o":["He gave it to the school.","He took it home.","He left it where he had found it."],"a":2,"h":"The school was closed.","r":"He left it where he found it."},{"q":"Rona: why did her friend ask her not to tell anyone?","o":["She thought it would make things worse.","She wanted to keep it a surprise.","She didn’t know the classmates."],"a":0,"h":"Not long after, she started missing school.","r":"She thought it would make things worse."},{"q":"Bella: what did she realise at the bus stop?","o":["She had missed her bus.","She had only been charged for one item, not two.","She had left her bag in the café."],"a":1,"h":"A drink and a sandwich.","r":"She had been charged for only one item."},{"q":"Why didn’t Bella go back to the café?","o":["She didn’t care.","The café was closed.","She could see her bus coming and didn’t want to miss it."],"a":2,"h":"She worried the girl might have got into trouble.","r":"She didn’t want to miss her bus."}]},{"i":"🧪","n":"03 · Third conditional","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"If + past perfect, would have + past participle.","items":[{"q":"If Brandon ___ the money to a teacher, he might have found its owner.","o":["had given","would have given","has given"],"a":0,"h":"If-clause: had + V3.","r":"had given"},{"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["If I would have known, I would have helped.","If I had known, I would have helped.","If I knew, I would have helped."],"a":1,"h":"No would in the if-clause.","r":"If I had known…"},{"q":"What would you have done ___ you had been in my position?","o":["when","unless","if"],"a":2,"h":"Reverse order is possible.","r":"if"},{"q":"Third conditional talks about …","o":["imagined situations in the past","habits","real future plans"],"a":0,"h":"Things that did not happen.","r":"imagined past situations"}]},{"i":"😔","n":"If only","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"If only + had + V3 shows regret.","items":[{"q":"If only I ___ my friend to speak to a teacher.","o":["would have persuaded","had persuaded","persuade"],"a":1,"h":"had + V3.","r":"had persuaded"},{"q":"If Bella had gone back, she ___ the bill.","o":["had corrected","could correct","could have corrected"],"a":2,"h":"Result: could have + V3.","r":"could have corrected"}]},{"i":"🧩","n":"04 · Sentence builder","t":"mcq","x":5,"ctx":"EX 2. Match each beginning with the ending.","items":[{"q":"If she had looked more carefully at the bill, …","o":["she would have noticed that there was a mistake.","the waitress might have got into trouble.","we would have known who to give it to."],"a":0,"h":"She did not look carefully.","r":"she would have noticed the mistake"},{"q":"If we had seen someone drop the money in the field, …","o":["she would have noticed that there was a mistake.","we would have known who to give it to.","she might not have got so upset and missed school."],"a":1,"h":"The money’s owner.","r":"we would have known who to give it to"},{"q":"If only I had persuaded my friend to talk to her parents or a teacher, …","o":["we would have known who to give it to.","the waitress might have got into trouble.","she might not have got so upset and missed school."],"a":2,"h":"Rona’s friend.","r":"she might not have got so upset and missed school"},{"q":"If I had gone back to the café to explain the problem, …","o":["the waitress might have got into trouble.","she would have noticed that there was a mistake.","she might not have got so upset and missed school."],"a":0,"h":"Bella’s dilemma.","r":"the waitress might have got into trouble"}]},{"i":"🎬","n":"05 · Watch: the lost money dilemma","t":"mcq","x":3,"tr":"5.3","ctx":"🎬 Thay cho Track 36. Xem phần đầu (Keep or Return Lost Money?) của video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-J1CJH2g6xs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline text-blue-600\">Keep or Return Lost Money? & Teen Bans at Malls</a> (Speak English Through Real-Life Debates). Video có thêm phần Teen Bans at Malls: em không cần xem phần đó. Bật phụ đề tiếng Anh nếu cần. What would the speakers have done?","items":[{"q":"EX 3. What does the person find in the park?","o":["A phone.","A wad of cash that totals $100.","A bike."],"a":1,"h":"A wad of cash.","r":"A wad of cash, $100"},{"q":"Why would the money be so useful to him / her?","o":["To pay school fees.","To buy a present for a friend.","To buy a new bike for the citywide bike race."],"a":2,"h":"His/her bike is old.","r":"To buy a new bike for the race"},{"q":"How does the person feel after a while?","o":["Guilty — he / she thinks about how unhappy the owner must be.","Very proud.","Not interested."],"a":0,"h":"Pretty soon he / she starts to feel …","r":"Guilty"},{"q":"What does the first speaker say about the money?","o":["Take it and run.","Give it back: if it’s not yours, turn it over to the police.","Spend it quickly."],"a":1,"h":"Giving the money back is the only thing to do.","r":"Give it back / turn it over to the police"},{"q":"What reasons does the second speaker give for keeping it?","o":["The money belongs to the park.","The police would keep it.","The owner was irresponsible or so rich they don’t care; it’s a dog-eat-dog world."],"a":2,"h":"Take the money and run.","r":"Irresponsible or rich owner; dog-eat-dog world"}]},{"i":"🗒️","n":"What would they have done?","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":12,"oc":1,"tr":"5.3","h":"🗒️ EX 3. Dựa vào video, viết điều mỗi người sẽ làm và lý do. Dùng: would have / wouldn’t have.","items":[["🔙","a","What would the first speaker have done with the money? Why?","The first speaker would have … because …",["would have","because"],"would|because"],["💨","b","What would the second speaker have done? Why?","The second speaker would have … because …",["would have","because"],"would|because"],["🤔","c","(Brandon’s dilemma in your book is similar.) What do you think is the better choice here?","I think the better choice is … because …",["because"],"because|think"]]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"06 · What would you have done?","t":"book","lbl":"EX 4","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"h":"🗣️ EX 4. Choose, then justify. There is no single correct choice.","items":[["💰","1","Brandon: you find money on the school field. The school is closed.","I would have … because …",["I would have","I wouldn’t have","I might have"],"would have|wouldn.t have|might have"],["🤐","2","Rona: a friend asks you to keep a secret about bullying.","I would have … because …",["I would have","I wouldn’t have","I might have"],"would have|wouldn.t have|might have"],["☕","3","Bella: the café charged you for one item only. Your bus is leaving.","I would have … because …",["I would have","I wouldn’t have","I might have"],"would have|wouldn.t have|might have"]]},{"i":"🛠️","n":"Final plan","t":"book","lbl":"PLAN","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🛠️ SCENARIO: you promised to keep a secret. Later you realised someone was being treated unfairly. You told no one and now you regret it (hypothetical case).","items":[["1️⃣","1","Decision","I would have … (spoken to a trusted adult / encouraged my friend to seek help / …)",["I would have"],"would have"],["2️⃣","2","Reason","I would have done this because …",[],"because"],["3️⃣","3","Third conditional","If I had …, I would / could / might have …",[],"if .* had .* have"],["4️⃣","4","If only","If only I had …",[],"if only .* had"]]},{"i":"☕","n":"Bella’s story","t":"order","x":14,"items":[0],"h":"☕ Put Bella’s story in the right order.","hint":"Follow the text of the post.","cards":["A. She paid the bill and left.","B. She had a drink and a sandwich at a café in town.","C. She got on the bus and went home.","D. She remembered that the waitress was young and new to the job.","E. She worried that the waitress might have got into trouble.","F. At the bus stop she realised she had been charged for one item, not two.","G. She saw her bus coming and didn’t want to miss it."],"ans":[1,0,5,3,6,2,4],"yl":"☕ YOUR TIMELINE","ft":"☕ TIMELINE SET","flow":["CAFÉ","PAID","REALISED","THOUGHT OF THE WAITRESS","THE BUS","WENT HOME","WORRY"],"bm":"Not quite. Go from the café to the bus stop to the worry at the end."},{"i":"💭","n":"Real or imagined?","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"💭 Did it really happen, or is it imagined?","hint":"Third conditional and if only talk about things that did NOT happen.","lab":["✅ WHAT REALLY HAPPENED","💭 IMAGINED (did not happen)"],"items":[["She started missing school.",0],["I could see my bus coming and I didn’t want to miss it.",0],["I got on the bus and went home.",0],["If only I had told a teacher, the teacher would have sorted it out.",1],["If someone had lost the money, they would have gone back to look for it.",1],["I picked up the money but didn’t know what to do with it.",0]],"sg":"💡 The if-clause with had + past participle is the signal for an imagined past."},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Moral dilemma solver","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Write your final answer about the secret scenario: your decision, a reason, one third conditional sentence and one if-only sentence.","hint":"I would have … because … If I had …, I would have … If only I had …","ph":"I would have spoken to a trusted adult because … If I had told someone, … would have … If only I had …","checks":[["Clear decision","would have|wouldn.t have|might have",1],["Gives a reason","because|so that|since",1],["Third conditional (if + had + V3, would have)","if .*had [a-z]+.*(would|could|might) have",1],["If only + past perfect","if only .*had [a-z]+",1],["Clear and complete (a full paragraph)",".{100,}",1]],"sk":["I can explain what a moral dilemma is.","I can identify the three dilemmas and explain the writers’ attitudes.","I can form third conditional sentences.","I can use would have, could have and might have + past participle.","I can use if only + past perfect to express regret."]}],"mx":199};
MX["5.4"]={"code":"06.5","title":"The Teen Rights Investigator","q":"Discover your rights. Understand your responsibilities. · ADULT? → READ → COLLOCATIONS → DEBATE → RESEARCH → REPORT","end":{"t":"📜 MISSION COMPLETE – TEEN RIGHTS INVESTIGATOR","did":"You explored age-related rights in the UK list, learned seven collocations, defended your opinion, researched teenagers’ rights in Vietnam and wrote a rights-and-responsibilities report. 🏅 Badge: TEEN RIGHTS INVESTIGATOR","r":"Every right comes with a responsibility, because …"},"steps":[{"i":"🎂","n":"01 · When are you an adult?","t":"think","x":4,"h":"🎂 GETTING STARTED. At what age are you considered to be an adult?","lab":["16","18","20","🟡 IT DEPENDS"],"items":[["Choose your opinion.",[0,1,2,3],"opinion"]],"pr":"Explain your opinion in one sentence.","bt":"Lock my opinion","sg":"Locked! Now read the UK list in your book."},{"i":"🕵️","n":"02 · Age detective","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 1. According to the textbook list (UK), at what age can you …?","items":[{"q":"buy a pet?","o":["14","12","18"],"a":1,"h":"The youngest age in the list.","r":"12"},{"q":"open your own bank account?","o":["13","16","12"],"a":0,"h":"Teen years begin.","r":"13"},{"q":"work part-time (with your school’s permission)?","o":["16","18","14"],"a":2,"h":"Before 16.","r":"14"},{"q":"work full-time or join the army?","o":["17","16","18"],"a":1,"h":"The same age as leaving full-time education.","r":"16"},{"q":"learn to drive?","o":["17","18","14"],"a":0,"h":"One year after 16.","r":"17"},{"q":"vote, get married, give blood or do jury service?","o":["16","18","17"],"a":1,"h":"Adulthood in the list.","r":"18"}]},{"i":"😮","n":"What surprises you?","t":"book","lbl":"OPINION","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"😮 Does anything surprise you? Write at least two sentences.","items":[["💡","1","Something that surprised me","I was surprised that … / I didn’t know that …",["I was surprised that","I didn’t know that"],"surprised|didn.t know"],["⚖️","2","Is it reasonable?","I think it is reasonable / unreasonable because …",["reasonable","unreasonable"],"because"]]},{"i":"🧩","n":"03 · Build the collocations","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 2. Choose the collocation without looking at the reading.","items":[{"q":"work …","o":["part-time / full-time","married","a bank account"],"a":0,"h":"Job.","r":"work part-time"},{"q":"leave …","o":["the army","home","blood"],"a":1,"h":"Move out.","r":"leave home"},{"q":"get …","o":["jury service","blood","married"],"a":2,"h":"Wedding.","r":"get married"},{"q":"join …","o":["the army","home","blood"],"a":0,"h":"Military.","r":"join the army"},{"q":"open …","o":["married","a bank account","part-time"],"a":1,"h":"Bank.","r":"open a bank account"},{"q":"do …","o":["home","the army","jury service"],"a":2,"h":"Court duty.","r":"do jury service"},{"q":"give …","o":["blood","part-time","a bank account"],"a":0,"h":"Donate.","r":"give blood"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Use the collocations","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Extra practice (not from the book).","items":[{"q":"At 18, people in the textbook list can ___.","o":["open married","do jury service","give a bank account"],"a":1,"h":"Right collocation.","r":"do jury service"},{"q":"Some teenagers want to ___ while studying.","o":["leave blood","join married","work part-time"],"a":2,"h":"Job.","r":"work part-time"},{"q":"You need to visit a bank if you want to ___.","o":["open a bank account","do a bank account","get a bank account"],"a":0,"h":"Open.","r":"open a bank account"},{"q":"A person who donates blood can ___.","o":["do blood","give blood","open blood"],"a":1,"h":"Donate.","r":"give blood"}]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"04 · Are age limits fair?","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🗣️ EX 3. Discuss each statement in Ex 1 with a partner. Choose a position and justify it. There is no single correct answer.","items":[["🐶","1","Buying a pet at 12","I think it is reasonable because … / I don’t agree because …",["reasonable","I don’t agree"],"because"],["🏦","2","Opening a bank account at 13","In my opinion, … should be allowed to … because …",["In my opinion"],"because|opinion|think"],["💼","3","Part-time work at 14","I see your point, but … / It depends on …",["I see your point, but","It depends"],""],["🗳️","4","Voting at 18","Teenagers should be mature enough to …",["mature enough","responsibilities"],""]]},{"i":"⚖️","n":"Mini debate","t":"think","x":4,"h":"⚖️ STATEMENT: A person’s maturity is more important than their age when deciding what they should be allowed to do.","lab":["🟢 AGREE","🔴 DISAGREE","🟡 PARTLY AGREE"],"items":[["Choose your position.",[0,1,2],"position"]],"pr":"Why? Give one reason or example.","bt":"Lock my position","sg":"Locked! Good debating needs reasons."},{"i":"🔬","n":"05 · Research Vietnam","t":"book","lbl":"TOPIC","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"h":"🔬 EX 4. Research from reliable sources and write what you find. Do not assume Vietnam is the same as the UK. Add the source and any conditions.","items":[["📚","1","Education","In Vietnam, … (age, conditions, source)",["according to the source","in general"],""],["💼","2","Part-time work","In Vietnam, … (age, conditions, source)",["according to the source","subject to conditions"],""],["🏦","3","Bank account","In Vietnam, … (age, conditions, source)",["according to the source","subject to conditions"],""],["🚗","4","Driving","In Vietnam, … (age, conditions, source)",["according to the source"],""],["🗳️","5","Voting","In Vietnam, … (age, conditions, source)",["according to the source"],""],["💍","6","Marriage","In Vietnam, … (age, conditions, source)",["according to the source"],""]]},{"i":"🌏","n":"Compare two countries","t":"book","lbl":"COMPARE","sv":"Save","x":8,"min":25,"h":"🌏 Choose one topic (part-time work · bank accounts · driving · voting · marriage). Compare Vietnam with the UK list.","items":[["🔍","1","Write your comparison","Compared with the UK, … I think this rule is reasonable / should be reviewed because …",["Compared with the UK","However"],"compared with|however|whereas|while"]]},{"i":"🛠️","n":"Report plan","t":"book","lbl":"PLAN","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🛠️ STUDENT NEWSLETTER: What rights should teenagers have, and what responsibilities should come with them?","items":[["1️⃣","1","Choose a right (education · privacy · express opinions · safety and protection · another)","One important right is …",["the right to education","the right to privacy","the right to express opinions","the right to safety"],"right"],["2️⃣","2","Identify a related responsibility","This right comes with the responsibility to …",[],"responsib"],["3️⃣","3","Give a reason or example","For example, … / This is important because …",[],"for example|because"]]},{"i":"🎂","n":"Age sorter","t":"bucket","x":1,"h":"🎂 In the UK list, at what age can you do each thing?","hint":"Use the list in Exercise 1.","lab":["🐶 12–14","🧑 16","🚗 17","🗳️ 18"],"items":[["work full-time",1],["open your own bank account",0],["leave full-time education",1],["vote",3],["do jury service",3],["leave home (with your parents’ permission)",1],["join the army",1],["give blood",3],["learn to drive",2],["work part-time (with your school’s permission)",0],["own a house",3],["buy a pet",0],["get married",3]],"sg":"💡 Remember: these ages come from the textbook list for the UK."},{"i":"📝","n":"Write your country’s list","t":"order","x":8,"items":[0],"h":"📝 Put the writing task (Exercise 4) in order.","hint":"Research first, then write, then compare.","cards":["A. Compare what you’ve found with what other students have found.","B. Compare and discuss the differences between your country and the UK.","C. Find the information you need from the internet or other sources.","D. Write your list."],"ans":[2,0,3,1],"yl":"📝 YOUR PLAN","ft":"📝 PLAN SET","flow":["RESEARCH","COMPARE FINDINGS","WRITE","COMPARE COUNTRIES"],"bm":"Not quite. You can’t write before you research, and you compare countries last."},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Rights reporter","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Write a short newsletter report (4–6 sentences) about one right and its responsibility.","hint":"One important right is … This comes with the responsibility to … For example, … This is important because …","ph":"One important right for teenagers is … With this right comes the responsibility to … For example, …","checks":[["Names a right","right",1],["Explains a responsibility","responsib",1],["Uses reliable information or a source","according to|source|in the uk|in vietnam|research|law",1],["Gives a reason or example","because|for example|for instance|such as",1],["Clear English (a full paragraph)",".{100,}",1]],"sk":["I can identify the age-related activities in the UK list from the textbook.","I can use the seven citizenship collocations correctly.","I can express and justify an opinion about age limits.","I can research and organise information about teenagers’ rights in Vietnam.","I can compare two countries and explain a difference."]}],"mx":196};
MX["5.5"]={"code":"06.6","title":"The Witness Detective","q":"Who saw what? · CASE FILE → READ → INCONSISTENCIES → PAST TENSES → VERDICT → REPORT","end":{"t":"🕵️ CASE CLOSED – WITNESS DETECTIVE","did":"You compared two witness statements, found inconsistencies, used past continuous, past simple and was/were going to, gave a reasoned verdict and wrote an incident report. 🏅 Badge: WITNESS DETECTIVE","r":"According to Witness A, … however Witness B says …"},"steps":[{"i":"🗂️","n":"01 · Enter the case","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"CASE FILE 06: A cyclist hit a car door. Two witnesses give different accounts. A witness is someone who sees an event happen.","items":[{"q":"When is it useful for a witness to give a formal statement?","o":["Only when the witness knows the people involved.","Only when the witness wants to blame someone.","When the police or another authority needs to understand what happened."],"a":2,"h":"Think about official investigations.","r":"When an authority needs to understand what happened."}]},{"i":"🔮","n":"02 · Predict the accident","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"h":"🔮 EX 1. Use the word bank to predict what might happen: parked car · wing mirror · selfie stick · handlebars · accident · crash into · fall off.","items":[["🚲","1","Complete your prediction","The cyclist might … because …",["crash into","fall off","selfie stick","handlebars"],"might"]]},{"i":"📰","n":"03 · Evidence scanner","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 2. Read both statements on page 132, then answer.","items":[{"q":"What was the cyclist holding in his left hand, according to Witness A?","o":["A phone on a selfie stick","A car key","A shopping bag"],"a":0,"h":"Check Witness A.","r":"A phone on a selfie stick"},{"q":"What was the cyclist wearing, according to Witness B?","o":["A silver jacket","A blue T-shirt and blue jeans","A red helmet and gloves"],"a":1,"h":"Check Witness B.","r":"A blue T-shirt and blue jeans"},{"q":"Which vehicle was involved, according to Witness A?","o":["A red car","A silver van","A silver Mercedes (car door)"],"a":2,"h":"Opening door.","r":"A silver Mercedes"},{"q":"What did the cyclist catch, according to Witness B?","o":["The van’s wing mirror","The car door","A phone"],"a":0,"h":"Mirror.","r":"The wing mirror of a silver van"}]},{"i":"⚖️","n":"Find the inconsistencies","t":"book","lbl":"COMPARE","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"h":"⚖️ Compare the two accounts (vehicle · helmet · cyclist’s action · what happened). Different details do not automatically prove someone is lying.","items":[["❌","1","Which details directly contradict each other?","The witnesses disagree about …",["vehicle","helmet","action"],"disagree|whereas|but"],["👀","2","Which details might reflect different viewpoints?","Witness A says …, whereas Witness B says …",["whereas"],""],["🧠","3","Which account seems more reliable? Why?","I think … because …",[],"because"]]},{"i":"🧪","n":"04 · Choose the tense","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Past continuous = action in progress. Past simple = event that interrupts it. Was/were going to = past intention.","items":[{"q":"I ___ along the road when a car door suddenly opened.","o":["am cycling","was cycling","cycled"],"a":1,"h":"Action in progress.","r":"was cycling"},{"q":"The cyclist was looking at his phone when someone ___ the door.","o":["opens","was opening","opened"],"a":2,"h":"Interrupting event.","r":"opened"},{"q":"He had his arm out to show that he ___ turn left.","o":["was going to","is going","went to"],"a":0,"h":"Past intention.","r":"was going to"},{"q":"When the car door opened, the cyclist ___ at his phone.","o":["looked","was looking","is looking"],"a":1,"h":"Background action.","r":"was looking"},{"q":"I ___ get my bag when a cyclist crashed into the door.","o":["was going","went to","was going to"],"a":2,"h":"Intention.","r":"was going to"},{"q":"He ___ a helmet, so he wasn’t badly hurt. (Witness B)","o":["was wearing","wears","wore"],"a":0,"h":"Background description.","r":"was wearing"}]},{"i":"✏️","n":"Exercise 3 · Complete the sentences (a–e)","t":"mcq","x":5,"ctx":"EX 3 (page 133). Use the past continuous or the past simple of the verbs in brackets.","items":[{"q":"a. I (cycle) ___ along the road when a car door suddenly (open) ___ in front of me.","o":["was cycling / was opening","was cycling / opened","cycled / was opening"],"a":1,"h":"Action in progress + interrupting event.","r":"was cycling … opened"},{"q":"b. I (hold) ___ the handlebars with my right hand when I (hit) ___ the car door.","o":["held / was hitting","was holding / was hitting","was holding / hit"],"a":2,"h":"Progress + interruption.","r":"was holding … hit"},{"q":"c. When the accident (happen) ___, I (carry) ___ my phone on a selfie stick.","o":["happened / was carrying","was happening / carried","happened / carried"],"a":0,"h":"Event + background.","r":"happened … was carrying"},{"q":"d. The cyclist (crash) ___ into the door as I (get) ___ out of the car.","o":["crashed / got","crashed / was getting","was crashing / got"],"a":1,"h":"Event + action in progress.","r":"crashed … was getting"},{"q":"e. I (not / pay) ___ attention when I (open) ___ the door.","o":["didn’t pay / was opening","wasn’t paying / was opening","wasn’t paying / opened"],"a":2,"h":"Progress + interruption.","r":"wasn’t paying … opened"}]},{"i":"🎯","n":"Exercise 3 · Past intention (f–h)","t":"mcq","x":5,"ctx":"EX 3 (page 133). Use going to show past intention (example f: I was going to get my bag…).","items":[{"q":"f. I (get) ___ my bag from the back of the car when a cyclist crashed into the door.","o":["was going to get","got","was getting to"],"a":0,"h":"Past intention.","r":"was going to get"},{"q":"g. We (exchange) ___ names and addresses, but a police officer arrived and took statements from us and from two witnesses.","o":["were exchanging","were going to exchange","exchanged"],"a":1,"h":"They intended to, but were interrupted.","r":"were going to exchange"},{"q":"h. I (send) ___ a video of my journey to college to my friends in Germany, but my phone got damaged in the accident.","o":["was sending","sent","was going to send"],"a":2,"h":"Intention that did not happen.","r":"was going to send"}]},{"i":"💭","n":"Your own past intention","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":12,"h":"💭 Write one sentence of your own with was / were going to about something you intended to do but didn’t.","items":[["📝","+","Your own sentence","I was going to … but …",["was going to","were going to"],"(was|were) going to"]]},{"i":"⚖️","n":"05 · Who was responsible?","t":"think","x":5,"h":"⚖️ EX 4. Who was responsible for the accident, the driver or the cyclist?","lab":["🚗 THE DRIVER","🚲 THE CYCLIST","🤝 BOTH SHARED","❓ NOT ENOUGH EVIDENCE"],"items":[["Your verdict",[0,1,2,3],"verdict"]],"pr":"Reason 1: use evidence (According to Witness A / Witness B …).","bt":"Lock my verdict","sg":"Locked! Add a second reason."},{"i":"🧩","n":"Support your verdict","t":"book","lbl":"REASON","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🧩 Give two reasons. Separate evidence from opinion.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Reason 1 (evidence)","According to Witness A, …",["According to Witness A","According to Witness B"],"according|witness"],["2️⃣","2","Reason 2 (opinion)","I think … because … / The cyclist should have …",["should have","We cannot be certain because"],"because|should"]]},{"i":"🚲","n":"What Witness A saw","t":"order","x":12,"items":[0],"h":"🚲 Put Witness A’s account of the accident in order.","hint":"Follow the story from the driver’s view.","cards":["A. Someone in a silver Mercedes opened the car door.","B. He wasn’t badly hurt.","C. The cyclist was looking at the phone on his selfie stick.","D. He fell off his bike.","E. The driver was driving behind the cyclist.","F. The cyclist didn’t see the door and hit it."],"ans":[4,2,0,5,3,1],"yl":"🚲 YOUR TIMELINE","ft":"🚲 TIMELINE SET","flow":["DRIVING","CYCLIST’S PHONE","DOOR OPENS","HITS THE DOOR","FALLS","NOT BADLY HURT"],"bm":"Not quite. The door opens before the cyclist hits it."},{"i":"🕵️","n":"Who said it?","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"🕵️ Which witness says each thing?","hint":"Check the two statements on page 132.","lab":["🚗 WITNESS A","🚶 WITNESS B"],"items":[["He was wearing a blue T-shirt and blue jeans.",1],["I was driving along the road behind the cyclist.",0],["The cyclist got too close to a silver van behind a red car.",1],["He had a phone on a selfie stick in his left hand.",0],["He was wearing a helmet.",1],["He wasn’t wearing a helmet.",0],["He had his arm out to show he was going to turn left.",1],["A silver Mercedes opened the car door.",0]],"sg":"💡 The witnesses disagree about the vehicle and the helmet."},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Incident report","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 You are the investigator. Write a short report using information from both witnesses.","hint":"Include: 2 past continuous · 1 interrupting past simple · 1 was/were going to · 1 inconsistency · your conclusion with a reason.","ph":"The cyclist was riding along the road when … Witness A says …, whereas Witness B says … I think … because …","checks":[["2+ past continuous sentences","(was|were) [a-z]+ing",2],["Past simple interrupting event","when .*(opened|hit|caught|crashed|fell)|(opened|hit|caught|crashed|fell) .*(when|as)",1],["Uses was/were going to","(was|were) going to",1],["Names an inconsistency","disagree|whereas|but witness|inconsisten|contradict|however",1],["Conclusion with a reason","(i think|in my opinion|conclusion).*because|because",1]],"sk":["I can explain what a witness does.","I can identify inconsistencies between two accounts.","I can use past continuous for an action in progress.","I can use past simple for an event that interrupts another action.","I can use was/were going to for a past intention.","I can express and support an opinion about responsibility."]}],"mx":167};
MX["5.6"]={"code":"06.7","title":"The Email Exchange Mission","q":"Can you write a polite but friendly reply? · INBOX → EMAIL DETECTIVE → TONE TRACKER → READ THE REPLY → TOOLKIT → WRITE","end":{"t":"📧 MISSION COMPLETE – EMAIL EXCHANGE EXPERT","did":"You identified the purpose and tone of an email, studied a model reply, practised polite expressions and wrote your own reply about school rules. 🏅 Badge: EMAIL EXCHANGE EXPERT","r":"A good email is polite, friendly and organised, because …"},"steps":[{"i":"📬","n":"01 · Open the inbox","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"New message. From: Isabel · Subject: School rules around the world. Isabel is a Year 9 student at Mira Flores International School doing a project about schools around the world.","items":[{"q":"What is the purpose of Isabel’s email?","o":["To ask Anisha about her school’s rules for an international project.","To complain about her school’s rules.","To invite Anisha to visit her school."],"a":0,"h":"Compare school rules.","r":"To ask about school rules for a project"}]},{"i":"🕵️","n":"02 · Email detective","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 1. Read Isabel’s email on page 134.","items":[{"q":"Who is Isabel writing to?","o":["Her English teacher","Anisha","The headteacher"],"a":1,"h":"Check the greeting.","r":"Anisha"},{"q":"Why is she writing?","o":["To complain about students’ behaviour.","To invite Anisha to her school.","To compare school rules in different countries."],"a":2,"h":"Project.","r":"To compare school rules"}]},{"i":"🎚️","n":"Tone tracker","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 2. Think about tone.","items":[{"q":"How would you describe the tone of Isabel’s email?","o":["Quite formal but friendly","Very formal","Very informal"],"a":0,"h":"Polite, not stiff.","r":"Quite formal but friendly"}]},{"i":"🔍","n":"Tone tracker · Explain","t":"book","lbl":"EX 2","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🔍 Answer in your own words using the email.","items":[["🙏","B","Which sentence in the opening is particularly polite, and why?","The sentence … is polite because …",["I would be very grateful if you could"],"because|grateful"],["😊","C","How does Isabel make the closing sound friendly and polite?","She uses … and … to sound …",["looking forward to hearing","I’d appreciate"],""],["¶","D","Why does the email have several short paragraphs?","Short paragraphs help the reader …",[],"reader|easy|help"]]},{"i":"📨","n":"03 · Read the reply","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"EX 3. Read Anisha’s reply on page 135.","items":[{"q":"Does Anisha answer Isabel’s questions about school rules?","o":["No, she only gives her personal opinion.","Yes, she addresses all the main topics.","No, she only talks about the school uniform."],"a":1,"h":"Arrival, uniform, classroom, outside, bullying, opinion.","r":"Yes, all main topics"},{"q":"What does Anisha think of the rules overall?","o":["Far too strict.","She has no opinion.","Quite reasonable, because they help the school be well-organised."],"a":2,"h":"Last paragraph.","r":"Quite reasonable"},{"q":"What does a late student have to do at Anisha’s school?","o":["Report to the school secretary, then go to the tutor group","Go home","Wait outside"],"a":0,"h":"Arrival and lateness.","r":"Report to the school secretary"}]},{"i":"🧰","n":"Polite expressions","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"Match each expression from Anisha’s email with its function.","items":[{"q":"“Thank you for your email.”","o":["Offering help","Thanking","Giving an opinion"],"a":1,"h":"Think about what the sentence does.","r":"Thanking"},{"q":"“I would be delighted to answer your questions …”","o":["Closing politely","Introducing a topic","Offering help"],"a":2,"h":"Think about what the sentence does.","r":"Offering help"},{"q":"“When it comes to the classroom …”","o":["Introducing a topic","Giving an opinion","Thanking"],"a":0,"h":"Think about what the sentence does.","r":"Introducing a topic"},{"q":"“Overall, I think that …”","o":["Closing politely","Giving an opinion","Offering help"],"a":1,"h":"Think about what the sentence does.","r":"Giving an opinion"},{"q":"“I hope my answers are helpful.”","o":["Introducing a topic","Thanking","Closing politely"],"a":2,"h":"Think about what the sentence does.","r":"Closing politely"}]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Ex 3 · Questions about Anisha’s reply","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🔎 EX 3 (page 135). Read Anisha’s reply, then answer the five questions in your own words.","items":[["a","a","Does Anisha answer all of Isabel’s questions?","Yes, she answers … topics: …",[],""],["b","b","Which sentences does Anisha use to make her reply sound polite and helpful?","She uses … and …",["Thank you for your email","I would be delighted","I hope my answers are helpful"],""],["c","c","Does Anisha include any personal opinions or information? If so, what are they?","Yes, she says …",[],""],["d","d","What impression do you get of Anisha and her attitude towards her school?","I think Anisha is … because …",[],"because|think"],["e","e","What is your impression of Anisha’s school?","I think the school is …",["strict","well-organised","reasonable"],""]]},{"i":"🗺️","n":"04 · Plan your reply","t":"book","lbl":"PLAN","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":8,"h":"🗺️ Plan notes for each topic, in the same order as Isabel’s questions.","items":[["⏰","1","Arrival time and what happens if students are late","We are expected to … If a student is late, …",["expected to","have to"],""],["👔","2","Uniform, hairstyles and jewellery","We have to wear … We’re not allowed to …",["not allowed to"],""],["📱","3","Classroom behaviour and mobile phones","In the classroom, we’re expected to …",[],""],["🏃","4","Rules outside the classroom","Outside the classroom, …",[],""],["🛡️","5","Anti-bullying rules and what I would do","If I saw someone being bullied, I would …",["would"],"would"],["💭","6","My overall opinion","Overall, I think … because …",["Overall, I think"],"because"]]},{"i":"✉️","n":"Build Anisha’s email","t":"order","x":16,"items":[0],"h":"✉️ Put the parts of the email in a sensible order.","hint":"Greeting → thanks → answers in the same order as the questions → opinion → closing.","cards":["A. I hope my answers are helpful. Best wishes, Anisha","B. Yes, we do have to wear a school uniform …","C. When it comes to the classroom, we’re expected to be polite …","D. Outside the classroom, we can move around … quite freely …","E. We are expected to arrive at school by 8.30 a.m. …","F. Thank you for your email … I would be delighted to answer your questions.","G. Dear Isabel,","H. Overall, I think that our rules are quite reasonable …","I. In terms of anti-bullying policies, we are encouraged to report …"],"ans":[6,5,4,1,2,3,8,7,0],"yl":"✉️ YOUR EMAIL ORDER","ft":"✉️ EMAIL READY","flow":["GREETING","THANKS","ARRIVAL","UNIFORM","CLASSROOM","OUTSIDE","ANTI-BULLYING","OPINION","CLOSING"],"bm":"Not quite. Answer in the order Isabel asked, then give your opinion, then close politely."},{"i":"🧰","n":"Polite expression sorter","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"🧰 Sort each expression by its function in the email.","hint":"Opening · introducing a topic · giving an opinion · closing.","lab":["👋 OPENING","📌 INTRODUCING A TOPIC","💭 OPINION","🤝 CLOSING"],"items":[["I hope my answers are helpful.",3],["Overall, I think that our rules are quite reasonable.",2],["In terms of anti-bullying policies, …",1],["Thank you for your email.",0],["When it comes to the classroom, …",1],["I would be delighted to answer your questions.",0],["Best wishes,",3],["Outside the classroom, …",1]],"sg":"💡 These phrases make an email polite but friendly."},{"i":"✉️","n":"FINAL BOSS · Reply to Isabel","t":"final","px":10,"h":"✉️ EX 4. Write your reply to Isabel about the rules at your school. Start politely, answer in her order, give your opinion at the end and close politely. Model: Anisha’s email.","hint":"Dear Isabel, Thank you for your email. I’d be happy to … We are expected to … When it comes to … Overall, I think … I hope this information is helpful. Best wishes,","ph":"Dear Isabel,\n\nThank you for your email. I’d be happy to tell you about the rules at my school.\n\n…\n\nBest wishes,","checks":[["Polite, friendly opening","dear isabel|thank you|happy to|delighted",2],["Covers lateness / arrival","late|arrive|arrival",1],["Covers uniform and appearance","uniform|jewellery|hair",1],["Covers phones / classroom / bullying","phone|classroom|bully",2],["Gives an overall opinion with a reason","(overall|in my opinion|i think).*because|because",1],["Polite closing","i hope|best wishes|looking forward|helpful",1]],"sk":["I used a polite but friendly greeting.","I answered the questions in the original order.","I included information about the main school-rule topics.","I gave my own opinion and explained why.","I used paragraphs to organise my ideas.","I checked spelling, punctuation and grammar.","I ended the email politely."]}],"mx":154};
MX["5.7"]={"code":"06.8","title":"The Truth & Choices Challenge","q":"Discuss, respond and record. Organise facts and write a statement. · DECIDE → PREPARE → PERFORM → INVESTIGATE → WRITE → REFLECT","end":{"t":"🎙️ MISSION COMPLETE – TRUTH & CHOICES","did":"You discussed a moral dilemma, planned and recorded a podcast, told facts from opinions, wrote a witness statement in chronological order and reflected on your work. 🏅 Badge: TRUTH & CHOICES","r":"The hardest part was … because …"},"steps":[{"i":"📰","n":"Project 1 · Read the dilemma","t":"think","x":5,"h":"📰 PROJECT 1 (book p. 136). A friend’s secret: someone posted false information about her online. She asked you to keep it secret. Next day she stopped coming to school. If someone tells you something in confidence, should you always keep their secret? What would you have done?","lab":["🤐 KEEP THE SECRET","👩‍🏫 TELL A TRUSTED TEACHER","🤝 PERSUADE HER TO REPORT FIRST","❓ SOMETHING ELSE"],"items":[["What would you do as the narrator?",[0,1,2,3],"decision"]],"pr":"Why? Give one reason in English (try: I would have … because …).","bt":"Lock my decision","sg":"Locked! Now prepare your podcast."},{"i":"🧭","n":"Podcast planner","t":"book","lbl":"PLAN","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"h":"🧭 Fill in the podcast plan before you speak. No need to write a full script.","items":[["🎬","1","Opening: introduce the situation","Today we are discussing a dilemma: …",["Today we are discussing"],""],["💭","2","Your opinion","I would have … because …",["I would have","I wouldn’t have"],"would have|wouldn.t have|think"],["🔄","3","Another possible view","Another possible view is that …",["Another possible view is"],""],["🗣️","4","Respond to a group member","I see your point, but …",["I agree with you about","I see your point","I can see what you mean, but"],"agree|see your point|see what you mean|good point|right"]]},{"i":"🧰","n":"Speaking toolkit","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Useful expressions from the book.","items":[{"q":"Which expression disagrees politely?","o":["I can see what you mean, but …","That’s a good point …","I think you’re right …"],"a":0,"h":"Look for “but”.","r":"I can see what you mean, but …"},{"q":"You made a mistake while speaking. What can you say?","o":["I don’t care.","What I meant to say was …","I agree with you about …"],"a":1,"h":"Self-correct.","r":"What I meant to say was …"},{"q":"You want to check what someone meant. What can you ask?","o":["I see your point …","I agree with you about …","Did you mean to say …?"],"a":2,"h":"Clarify.","r":"Did you mean to say …?"}]},{"i":"🎙️","n":"Perform and reflect","t":"book","lbl":"RECORD","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":15,"oc":1,"h":"🎙️ Record your group conversation (phone or recorder), play it to the class, then reflect.","items":[["🎧","1","What did you find most interesting about the conversations?","I found … interesting because …",[],"because"],["🔁","2","Did you change any of your opinions after listening? Why?","I changed / didn’t change my opinion because …",["changed","didn’t change"],"because"]]},{"i":"🔥","n":"Project 2 · Fact or opinion?","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"PROJECT 2 (book p. 137): “Teenage girl saves family from fire” — Chantale woke around midnight, smelled smoke, woke her parents and carried her three-year-old sister out. Everyone escaped unhurt.","items":[{"q":"Chantale woke up at around midnight.","o":["Fact","Opinion"],"a":0,"h":"It is in the report.","r":"Fact"},{"q":"The fire was the most frightening experience of her life.","o":["Fact","Opinion"],"a":1,"h":"Not in the report.","r":"Opinion"},{"q":"She carried her three-year-old sister downstairs.","o":["Fact","Opinion"],"a":0,"h":"In the report.","r":"Fact"},{"q":"Chantale was a perfect hero.","o":["Fact","Opinion"],"a":1,"h":"A judgment.","r":"Opinion"}]},{"i":"📋","n":"Evidence checklist","t":"mcq","x":4,"ctx":"A statement is written in chronological order. Chantale’s events from the report.","items":[{"q":"Which event comes first?","o":["Her family escaped unhurt.","She woke up at around midnight and smelled smoke.","She carried her sister out of the house."],"a":1,"h":"Start with the beginning.","r":"She woke up and smelled smoke."},{"q":"Which sentence should NOT be in the statement?","o":["I carried my sister out of the house.","I woke my parents.","I think the fire started because of a candle."],"a":2,"h":"Don’t invent details.","r":"Invented cause of the fire"},{"q":"The statement should be written from …","o":["Chantale’s point of view (I / my)","a reporter’s point of view","the police’s point of view"],"a":0,"h":"First person.","r":"Chantale’s point of view"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Write the statement","t":"book","lbl":"DRAFT","sv":"Save","x":10,"min":60,"h":"✍️ Write Chantale’s statement to the police in the first person, in chronological order, using only facts from the report.","items":[["📝","1","My police statement","I woke up at around midnight and … Then I … Finally, …",["I woke up","I smelled smoke","I carried","we escaped"],"\\bi\\b|\\bmy\\b"]]},{"i":"👀","n":"Peer review","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Check your draft (or a partner’s draft).","items":[{"q":"Which sentence is best for a statement?","o":["My sister was lucky to have such a hero.","I carried my sister down the stairs and out of the house.","I probably saved everyone’s life."],"a":1,"h":"Fact, first person.","r":"I carried my sister down the stairs…"},{"q":"Which checklist point is most important?","o":["The statement is as long as possible.","It includes new details to make it exciting.","The events are in chronological order."],"a":2,"h":"Order of events.","r":"Chronological order"}]},{"i":"🎙️","n":"Make a podcast","t":"order","x":10,"items":[0],"h":"🎙️ Put the steps of Project 1 in order.","hint":"Read → discuss → prepare → record → play.","cards":["A. Discuss what you would have done. Include as many different ideas as possible.","B. Prepare to record: decide who starts and the speaking order.","C. Work in small groups. Read and discuss the dilemma.","D. Play it to the class and ask which ideas they agree or disagree with.","E. Record your conversation."],"ans":[2,0,1,4,3],"yl":"🎙️ YOUR PODCAST PLAN","ft":"🎙️ PLAN SET","flow":["READ","DISCUSS","PREPARE","RECORD","PLAY"],"bm":"Not quite. You prepare before you record, and you play it at the end."},{"i":"📋","n":"Statement: do or don’t?","t":"bucket","x":2,"h":"📋 What should a witness statement do? Sort each tip.","hint":"Remember the four rules in Project 2.","lab":["✅ DO","❌ DON’T"],"items":[["Tell the story in chronological order.",0],["Give your opinion about who was right.",1],["Guess what caused the fire.",1],["Only give facts.",0],["Report anything you heard as accurately as possible.",0],["Say something you are not sure about.",1]],"sg":"💡 If you’re not sure of something, don’t say it."},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Reflection","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Final reflection (book p. 137). What did you find most challenging about writing a statement? Did this task make you think differently about how you remember or report a past event? Why?","hint":"The most challenging part was … This task made me think … because …","ph":"The most challenging part of writing a statement was … because … This task made me think … because …","checks":[["Names something challenging","challeng|difficult|hard",1],["Explains why","because|since|so that",1],["Refers to remembering or reporting events","remember|report|event|fact|opinion|order",1],["Reflects on thinking differently","think|realis|realiz|differently|more careful",1],["Clear English (a short paragraph)",".{80,}",1]],"sk":["I can explain the moral dilemma and give reasons for my decision.","I can respond to another person’s opinion politely.","I have prepared and recorded a group podcast.","I can distinguish facts from opinions.","I have written Chantale’s statement in chronological order.","I have reviewed and improved my final draft."]}],"mx":126};
MX["w5.0"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.1","title":"The School Rules Detective","q":"Can you use school-rules language and suggest fairer rules? · COMPLETE → OPINION → DESIGN RULES → PROPOSAL","end":{"t":"🕵️ SCHOOL RULES DETECTIVE – PRACTICE COMPLETE","did":"You completed the school-rules conversation, gave opinions with reasons, designed three new rules and proposed fairer rules. ✓ Vocabulary · ✓ Opinions · ✓ Rule design. Use of English p. 91 is in the next tab.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.2 – Family life."},"steps":[{"i":"🏫","n":"Warm-up · Do rules help?","t":"think","x":3,"h":"🏫 WARM-UP (web support). Do school rules help students?","lab":["🟢 YES, A LOT","🟡 SOME DO","🔴 NOT REALLY"],"items":[["Choose one.",[0,1,2],"opinion"]],"pr":"Give one reason (safety, respect, learning …).","bt":"Lock my answer","sg":"Locked! Now let’s learn the language of school rules."},{"i":"🗂️","n":"Word sorter · behaviour and consequences","t":"bucket","x":1,"h":"🗂️ SORT THE EXPRESSIONS. Is it good behaviour, breaking the rules, or a consequence?","hint":"Think: what students do → what happens next.","lab":["🌟 GOOD BEHAVIOUR","🚫 BREAKING THE RULES","⚖️ CONSEQUENCES"],"items":[["bring a note from your parents when absent",0],["show respect for others",0],["stay behind after school",2],["get a detention",2],["shout or run in the corridors",1],["get into trouble",2],["get plus points for good behaviour",0],["break the rules",1],["get a verbal warning",2],["get minus points",2]],"sg":"💡 Notice the pattern: break the rules → warning → detention."},{"i":"📖","n":"Vocabulary · What does it mean?","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Choose the best definition.","items":[{"q":"strict","o":["very friendly and relaxed","making people obey the rules firmly","new and modern"],"a":1,"h":"A strict school has firm rules.","r":"strict = firm about rules"},{"q":"respect (for others)","o":["behaving politely because you value other people","being afraid of someone","being better than other people"],"a":0,"h":"show respect for others.","r":"respect = polite behaviour towards others"},{"q":"good behaviour","o":["a school subject","a type of uniform","acting politely and following the rules"],"a":2,"h":"Plus points are given for it.","r":"good behaviour = polite, follows the rules"},{"q":"a verbal warning","o":["a warning that someone says to you","a warning written on paper","a prize for good work"],"a":0,"h":"verbal = spoken.","r":"verbal = spoken"},{"q":"a detention","o":["a school trip","a punishment: you have to stay at school after lessons","a free lesson"],"a":1,"h":"You stay behind after school.","r":"detention = staying after school as a punishment"},{"q":"stay behind","o":["to walk ahead of other people","to arrive early","to remain somewhere after other people have left"],"a":2,"h":"stay behind after school.","r":"stay behind = remain after others leave"}]},{"i":"💬","n":"Ex 1 · Complete the conversation","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 88, Exercise 1. Word bank: behaviour · break · detention · respect · stay behind · strict · trouble · warning. In your book, gap 1 (strict) is the example. Sentences are shortened; check the full speech bubbles.","items":[{"q":"1. Do you have a lot of rules in your school? Is your school very ___?","o":["behaviour","strict","trouble"],"a":1,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"strict"},{"q":"2. I think that’s to show ___ for others.","o":["stay behind","trouble","respect"],"a":2,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"respect"},{"q":"3. … or you’ll get into ___.","o":["trouble","break","warning"],"a":0,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"trouble"},{"q":"4. We get plus points for good ___ every week …","o":["respect","behaviour","break"],"a":1,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"behaviour"},{"q":"5. Yes, if you ___ the rules …","o":["stay behind","detention","break"],"a":2,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"break"},{"q":"6. … or you have to ___ after school.","o":["stay behind","strict","warning"],"a":0,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"stay behind"},{"q":"7. After three warnings, you get a ___!","o":["respect","detention","strict"],"a":1,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"detention"},{"q":"8. … they always give you a verbal ___.","o":["behaviour","detention","warning"],"a":2,"h":"Read the whole sentence.","r":"warning"}]},{"i":"🪜","n":"The discipline ladder","t":"order","x":10,"items":[0],"h":"🪜 Put the steps in order, from breaking a rule to staying after school.","hint":"A verbal warning comes before a detention. Think about the bubbles in Exercise 1.","cards":["A. The student has to stay behind after school.","B. A student breaks the rules.","C. After three warnings, the student gets a detention.","D. The teacher gives a verbal warning."],"ans":[1,3,2,0],"yl":"🪜 YOUR LADDER","ft":"🪜 LADDER BUILT","flow":["BREAK A RULE","VERBAL WARNING","DETENTION","STAY BEHIND"],"bm":"Not quite. First a rule is broken, then a verbal warning, then a detention, and then the student stays behind."},{"i":"✅","n":"Check with the bubbles","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Facts from the speech bubbles in Exercise 1 (page 88).","items":[{"q":"What are students expected to do if they are absent?","o":["Phone the school","Do extra homework","Bring a note from their parents"],"a":2,"h":"Or they will get into trouble.","r":"Bring a note from their parents."},{"q":"What do students get every week for good behaviour?","o":["Plus points, and it goes on their report","A free lesson","A school trip"],"a":0,"h":"It encourages them to behave well.","r":"Plus points on their report."},{"q":"What mustn’t students do in the corridors?","o":["Walk or talk quietly","Shout or run","Carry bags"],"a":1,"h":"The student says it shows respect for others.","r":"They mustn’t shout or run."},{"q":"What do teachers always give before a detention?","o":["A prize","A plus point","A verbal warning"],"a":2,"h":"The teachers are quite nice.","r":"A verbal warning."}]},{"i":"💭","n":"Ex 2 · Your opinion","t":"book","lbl":"EX 2","sv":"Save","x":3,"min":15,"h":"💭 Workbook Exercise 2. Complete the three sentences with your own ideas. Add a reason or example to make a stronger answer (because · so that · in order to).","items":[["a","a","Why are school rules important?","I think school rules are important because …",["because","so that","I believe that"],"because|so that|in order to"],["b","b","What is one important rule?","One important rule is …",["Students should …","Students must …"],"rule"],["c","c","Which rule would you change?","One rule I would change is … because …",["I think it would be fairer if","Students should be allowed to"],"change|fairer|should"]]},{"i":"🧩","n":"Language support · give reasons","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Choose the best word or phrase to give a reason or a suggestion.","items":[{"q":"I think school rules are important ___ they keep students safe.","o":["but","because","although"],"a":1,"h":"A reason.","r":"because"},{"q":"We need rules ___ everyone can learn without being disturbed.","o":["so that","although","unless"],"a":0,"h":"Purpose.","r":"so that"},{"q":"Students wear a uniform ___ show they belong to the school.","o":["in order","so as that","in order to"],"a":2,"h":"Purpose + verb.","r":"in order to"},{"q":"I think it would be ___ if students could choose their break time.","o":["fair","fairer","the fairest"],"a":1,"h":"Comparative.","r":"fairer"}]},{"i":"🔧","n":"Improve my answer","t":"book","lbl":"MINI","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":25,"h":"🔧 MINI CHALLENGE. Take one of your answers from Exercise 2 and make it stronger: add a reason and an example. Basic: I think school rules are important because they keep students safe. Extended: … because they keep students safe and help everyone learn without being disturbed.","items":[["✍️","+","Write your extended answer","I think … because … and …",["because","so that","for example"],"because|so that|for example|such as"]]},{"i":"🛠️","n":"Challenge Ex 3 · Rule designer","t":"book","lbl":"RULE","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":25,"h":"🛠️ Challenge Exercise 3. Write three new rules for your school or class and say how each one will improve student behaviour. Check: clear · realistic · helps students learn or behave better · explains why it is useful.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Rule 1 and how it improves behaviour","Rule: … It will improve behaviour because …",["Students should …","The school should introduce …","Students shouldn’t have to …"],"because|will|improve|help"],["2️⃣","2","Rule 2 and how it improves behaviour","Rule: … It will improve behaviour because …",[],"because|will|improve|help"],["3️⃣","3","Rule 3 and how it improves behaviour","Rule: … It will improve behaviour because …",[],"because|will|improve|help"]]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Rule check","t":"chk","x":5,"items":[0],"h":"🔎 IS YOUR RULE EFFECTIVE? Tick each point for your three rules.","list":["The rule is clear and easy to understand.","The rule is realistic for a school or classroom.","The rule helps students learn or behave better.","I have explained why the rule is useful."]},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Fair rules proposal","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Your school wants to improve its rules. Propose one new rule, one rule that should be changed, and explain why your proposal is fair.","hint":"A new rule: … A rule I would change: … This is fair because …","ph":"A new rule could be … A rule I would change is … because … I think my proposal is fair because …","checks":[["Proposes a new rule","new rule|should introduce|should be|students should",1],["Names a rule to change","change|instead|rather than|should not|shouldn.t",1],["Gives a reason","because|so that|in order to",1],["Explains fairness","fair|everyone|all students|equal",1],["Clear English (a short paragraph)",".{90,}",1]],"sk":["I can use all eight school-rules vocabulary items.","I can express my opinion and give a reason.","I can create rules and explain their benefits.","I understand the structure be + past participle + to-infinitive.","I can complete the present simple passive sentences."]}],"mx":103};
MX["w5.1"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.2","title":"The Time-Management Coach","q":"Can you manage your time like a coach? · WARM-UP → ARTICLE GAPS → UNDERSTAND → VOCABULARY → WEEKLY PLAN","end":{"t":"⏱️ TIME-MANAGEMENT COACH – PRACTICE COMPLETE","did":"You completed the time-management article, understood its main ideas, matched seven key words and built a simple weekly plan. ✓ Article gaps · ✓ Comprehension · ✓ Vocabulary · ✓ Planning.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.3 – House rules."},"steps":[{"i":"⏳","n":"Warm-up · Where does your time go?","t":"think","x":3,"h":"⏳ WARM-UP (web support). When you have a lot of homework, what do you usually do?","lab":["📝 START AND MAKE A PLAN","🍰 EASIEST TASKS FIRST","😰 PUT IT OFF","🔀 SEVERAL TASKS AT ONCE"],"items":[["What do you usually do?",[0,1,2,3],"habit"]],"pr":"Is this a good way to manage time? Why / why not?","bt":"Lock my answer","sg":"Locked! Now read the article in your Workbook."},{"i":"🧩","n":"Ex 1 · Complete the article","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 89, Exercise 1. Word bank: as (×2) · be · for · in · like · of · sure · your · to. Use each word the number of times given.","items":[{"q":"1. In order to make the best use of your time, it’s a good idea ___ review your productivity regularly.","o":["to","like","be"],"a":0,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"to"},{"q":"2. …looking at all the activities… and making ___ that you are doing them as efficiently as possible.","o":["to","sure","for"],"a":1,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"sure"},{"q":"3. …doing them as efficiently ___ possible.","o":["of","for","as"],"a":2,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"as"},{"q":"4. …executives are usually trained to include this ___ their management practice.","o":["in","to","of"],"a":0,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"in"},{"q":"5. But this process can also ___ applied to studying…","o":["in","be","sure"],"a":1,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"be"},{"q":"6. …to studying, as well ___ everyday household tasks…","o":["for","of","as"],"a":2,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"as"},{"q":"7. …household tasks ___ cleaning and cooking.","o":["like","as","sure"],"a":0,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"like"},{"q":"8. Make a list ___ tasks and decide which ones are most important.","o":["your","of","be"],"a":1,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"of"},{"q":"9. Make a schedule ___ when you can reasonably complete each goal.","o":["like","your","for"],"a":2,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"for"},{"q":"10. If you study for too long without a break, ___ concentration will reduce…","o":["your","in","as"],"a":0,"h":"Read the whole sentence aloud.","r":"your"}]},{"i":"📖","n":"Understand the article","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Read the completed article (Workbook p. 89), then answer.","items":[{"q":"1. What does reviewing your productivity mean?","o":["Studying for as long as possible","Looking at your daily activities and how efficiently you do them","Doing every task at the same time"],"a":1,"h":"Look at the first paragraph.","r":"Looking at daily activities and efficiency"},{"q":"2. What should you do when setting goals?","o":["Set as many goals as possible","Avoid making a schedule","Set realistic goals and prioritise tasks"],"a":2,"h":"Second part.","r":"Set realistic goals and prioritise"},{"q":"3. Why should you break your workload into small steps?","o":["To reduce stress and build motivation","To make tasks more complicated","To increase stress"],"a":0,"h":"Small steps.","r":"To reduce stress and give motivation"},{"q":"4. Why are breaks important?","o":["They mean you do not need to plan","They help protect concentration and productivity","They make every task shorter"],"a":1,"h":"Last paragraph.","r":"They protect concentration and productivity"}]},{"i":"🔤","n":"Ex 2 · Match the definitions","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 89, Exercise 2. Match the bold words from Exercise 1 with the definitions.","items":[{"q":"a. A series of steps.","o":["efficient","executives","process"],"a":2,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"process"},{"q":"b. Amount of work.","o":["workload","system","productivity"],"a":0,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"workload"},{"q":"c. Does things quickly without wasting time.","o":["employees","efficient","executives"],"a":1,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"efficient"},{"q":"d. How much you achieve in a certain time period.","o":["system","process","productivity"],"a":2,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"productivity"},{"q":"e. Senior managers who make important decisions in a company.","o":["executives","workload","employees"],"a":0,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"executives"},{"q":"f. A set way of doing things.","o":["process","system","efficient"],"a":1,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"system"},{"q":"g. People who work for a company.","o":["productivity","workload","employees"],"a":2,"h":"Think about the definition.","r":"employees"}]},{"i":"🗓️","n":"My weekly time system","t":"book","lbl":"GOAL","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"🗓️ Apply the article. Start with three important tasks (study or household). Make realistic goals and say when you will complete each one.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Goal 1","My goal is to … by …",["review","complete","schedule"],""],["2️⃣","2","Goal 2","My goal is to … by …",[],""],["3️⃣","3","Goal 3","My goal is to … by …",[],""],["☕","4","When will you take a break? (after one task · after 25 minutes · at a planned time)","I will take a break …",["after completing one task","after 25 minutes of focused work","at a planned time"],"break"]]},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · My productivity plan","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Write your plan in 4–6 sentences: your three goals, a simple schedule and when you will take breaks. Explain why your plan is realistic.","hint":"First, I will … Then … I will take a break … This plan is realistic because …","ph":"My plan for this week: First, I will … Then I will … I will take a break … This plan is realistic because …","checks":[["Names goals or tasks","goal|task|homework|clean|cook|study|revise",1],["Includes a schedule or time","schedule|monday|tuesday|wednesday|thursday|friday|saturday|sunday|a\\.m\\.|p\\.m\\.|o.clock|minutes|every|each",1],["Plans a break","break|rest",1],["Explains why it is realistic","because|realistic|so that",1],["Clear English (a short paragraph)",".{90,}",1]],"sk":["I can complete the time-management article using the word bank.","I understand the seven key vocabulary items.","I can explain why realistic goals and breaks are useful.","I can create a simple, realistic plan for my tasks."]}],"mx":69};
MX["w5.2"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.3","title":"The Home Rules Investigator","q":"Whose rules are they? · WARM-UP → READ THE BLOGS → FIND THE WRITER → MY HOME RULES → FAIR RULES","end":{"t":"🏠 HOME RULES INVESTIGATOR – PRACTICE COMPLETE","did":"You read three blogs about home rules, matched each description to the right writer, used clue words as evidence, wrote about your own rules and designed fair house rules. ✓ Reading for detail · ✓ Matching · ✓ Writing about rules.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.4 – Doing the right thing."},"steps":[{"i":"🏡","n":"Warm-up · Rules at home","t":"book","lbl":"WARM-UP","sv":"Save","x":3,"min":12,"h":"🏡 WARM-UP (web support). Which rules do you have at home? Use have to / can / ask permission.","items":[["📋","1","Write two rules you have at home","At home I have to … and I’m not allowed to …",["finish my homework first","keep my bedroom tidy","help with chores","tell my parents where I’m going","ask permission before going out"],"have to|allowed|must|ask"]]},{"i":"📖","n":"Ex 1 · Read the blogs · Quick checks","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Workbook p. 90, Exercise 1. Read the three blogs in your book (Leila · Nabil · Danuta). Which rules are the same in your home?","items":[{"q":"Leila: what is she mainly talking about?","o":["Keeping the house clean and tidy","Going out with friends","Finishing homework before using a phone"],"a":0,"h":"Tidy bedrooms, beds, bathroom, vacuuming.","r":"Keeping the house clean and tidy"},{"q":"Nabil: when can he watch TV or use his phone?","o":["Only at weekends","Only after finishing his homework","Whenever he wants"],"a":1,"h":"Homework first.","r":"Only after finishing his homework"},{"q":"Danuta: which rule does she mention?","o":["She must clean the bathroom.","She must finish her homework before using her phone.","She must tell her parents about her plans and return before 9 p.m."],"a":2,"h":"Going out rules.","r":"Tell her parents about her plans and be home before 9 p.m."}]},{"i":"🕵️","n":"Ex 2 · Find the correct writer","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 90, Exercise 2. Write the correct name: Leila, Nabil or Danuta. Tip: find words or phrases in the blogs that mean the same as the words in the question.","items":[{"q":"a. Rules for going out.","o":["Danuta","Leila","Nabil"],"a":0,"h":"Find words with a similar meaning in the blogs.","r":"Danuta – where I’m going; what time I’ll be home"},{"q":"b. Household chores.","o":["Danuta","Leila","Nabil"],"a":1,"h":"Find words with a similar meaning in the blogs.","r":"Leila – cleaning the bathroom; doing the vacuuming"},{"q":"c. Screen time.","o":["Leila","Danuta","Nabil"],"a":2,"h":"Find words with a similar meaning in the blogs.","r":"Nabil – watch TV; look at my phone"},{"q":"d. Not wearing shoes at home.","o":["Leila","Nabil","Danuta"],"a":0,"h":"Find words with a similar meaning in the blogs.","r":"Leila – wears slippers"},{"q":"e. Asking permission.","o":["Nabil","Danuta","Leila"],"a":1,"h":"Find words with a similar meaning in the blogs.","r":"Danuta – make sure my parents are OK with it"},{"q":"f. Studying.","o":["Leila","Danuta","Nabil"],"a":2,"h":"Find words with a similar meaning in the blogs.","r":"Nabil – getting all my homework done"}]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Vocabulary detective","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Match the question wording with similar words in the blogs.","items":[{"q":"Household chores ≈","o":["cleaning the bathroom; doing the vacuuming","where I’m going; what time I’ll be home","watch TV; look at my phone"],"a":0,"h":"Jobs at home.","r":"cleaning the bathroom; doing the vacuuming"},{"q":"Screen time ≈","o":["wears slippers","watch TV; look at my phone","getting all my homework done"],"a":1,"h":"Screens.","r":"watch TV; look at my phone"},{"q":"Asking permission ≈","o":["getting all my homework done","doing the vacuuming","make sure my parents are OK with it"],"a":2,"h":"Parents agree.","r":"make sure my parents are OK with it"}]},{"i":"🧱","n":"Sentence patterns","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Patterns: have to + V · be allowed to + V · be strict about + noun / V-ing · make sure (that) + clause.","items":[{"q":"My dad is strict ___ me getting my homework done.","o":["about","with","to"],"a":0,"h":"Strict about…","r":"about"},{"q":"I’m not ___ to watch TV until my homework is done.","o":["allowing","allowed","allow"],"a":1,"h":"Passive.","r":"allowed"},{"q":"I have to ___ my parents are OK with it.","o":["making sure","make sure of","make sure"],"a":2,"h":"make sure + clause.","r":"make sure"},{"q":"I always ___ tell my parents where I’m going.","o":["have to","am have to","having to"],"a":0,"h":"have to + V.","r":"have to"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Ex 3 · Tell us about rules in your home","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":20,"h":"✍️ Workbook Exercise 3. Blog title: “Tell us about rules in your home. Do you have a lot of rules? Do you agree with them?” Answer in your own words.","items":[["📜","1","What rules do you have in your home?","I have to … / I’m not allowed to … / My parents expect me to …",["I have to","I’m not allowed to","My parents expect me to"],"have to|allowed|expect"],["🔢","2","Do you have a lot of rules?","Yes, quite a few. / No, not really. / There are a few important rules.",["quite a few","not really","a few important rules"],""],["⚖️","3","Do you agree with the rules? Why or why not?","I agree with … because … / I would change … because …",["I agree with","I think … is reasonable","I would change"],"because"]]},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL BOSS · Fair house rules","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 You and your family want to agree on new house rules. Propose three rules that are reasonable and respect everyone. Explain why they are fair.","hint":"Rule 1: … Rule 2: … Rule 3: … These rules are fair because …","ph":"Rule 1: Everyone has to … Rule 2: We’re allowed to … if … Rule 3: …. These rules are fair because …","checks":[["Rule 1","rule 1|1\\.|first",1],["Rule 2","rule 2|2\\.|second",1],["Rule 3","rule 3|3\\.|third",1],["Uses have to / allowed to / make sure","have to|allowed to|make sure|expected to",1],["Explains fairness","fair|because|everyone|respect",1]],"sk":["I can identify the main ideas in Leila’s, Nabil’s and Danuta’s blogs.","I can match all six descriptions to the correct writer.","I can answer questions about rules in my own home.","I can use have to, be allowed to and make sure in sentences."]}],"mx":63};
MX["u5.0"]={"code":"USE OF ENGLISH","title":"The Grammar Detective","q":"Passive verbs followed by the infinitive · DECODE → CHECK! → PRESENT SIMPLE PASSIVE → SUPPOSED TO → ASK ABOUT YOUR SCHOOL → REPORT","end":{"t":"🔎 THE GRAMMAR DETECTIVE – COMPLETE","did":"You decoded be + V3 + to + verb, found subjects and verbs, completed the present simple passive, told be supposed to from I suppose and asked questions about your school. ✓ Passive + infinitive · ✓ be supposed to · ✓ questions.","r":"After this lab, I can …"},"steps":[{"i":"🧬","n":"Grammar decoder","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Subject + be + V3 + to + V1. be expected to · be allowed to · be encouraged to · be asked to · be supposed to. Example: They expect students to wear a school uniform. → Students are expected to wear a school uniform.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence is the passive form of “They expect students to wear a school uniform”?","o":["Students are expecting wear a school uniform.","Students are expected to wear a school uniform.","Students expect to wear a school uniform."],"a":1,"h":"be + V3 + to.","r":"Students are expected to wear a school uniform."},{"q":"I ___ expected to be on time.","o":["are","is","am"],"a":2,"h":"I + am.","r":"am"},{"q":"He ___ not allowed to use his phone.","o":["is","am","are"],"a":0,"h":"He + is.","r":"is"},{"q":"___ we expected to do homework every day?","o":["Is","Are","Am"],"a":1,"h":"We + are.","r":"Are"}]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Check! 1 · Subject and verb (1–4)","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 91, Check! Exercise 1. Read the poster rules. Underline the subject and circle the main verb in your book. In commands the subject (you) is understood.","items":[{"q":"1. “We’re expected to be punctual and polite.” Subject?","o":["polite","punctual","We"],"a":2,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"We"},{"q":"1. “We’re expected to be punctual and polite.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["’re expected (to be)","punctual","polite"],"a":0,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"’re expected (to be)"},{"q":"2. “Be punctual and polite.” Subject?","o":["polite","you (understood)","punctual"],"a":1,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"you (understood)"},{"q":"2. “Be punctual and polite.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["polite","punctual","be"],"a":2,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"be"},{"q":"3. “Listen to each other.” Subject?","o":["you (understood)","each other","listen"],"a":0,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"you (understood)"},{"q":"3. “Listen to each other.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["each","listen","other"],"a":1,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"listen"},{"q":"4. “Please don’t interrupt.” Subject?","o":["interrupt","please","you (understood)"],"a":2,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"you (understood)"},{"q":"4. “Please don’t interrupt.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["don’t interrupt","please","you"],"a":0,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"don’t interrupt"}]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Check! 1 · Subject and verb (5–8)","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 91, Check! Exercise 1, sentences 5–8.","items":[{"q":"5. “Share your ideas.” Subject?","o":["ideas","you (understood)","your"],"a":1,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"you (understood)"},{"q":"5. “Share your ideas.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["ideas","your","share"],"a":2,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"share"},{"q":"6. “Work together.” Subject?","o":["you (understood)","together","work"],"a":0,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"you (understood)"},{"q":"6. “Work together.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["you","work","together"],"a":1,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"work"},{"q":"7. “We’re not allowed to interrupt.” Subject?","o":["allowed","interrupt","We"],"a":2,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"We"},{"q":"7. “We’re not allowed to interrupt.” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["’re not allowed (to interrupt)","interrupt","not"],"a":0,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"’re not allowed (to interrupt)"},{"q":"8. “Are we expected to do homework every day?” Subject?","o":["day","we","homework"],"a":1,"h":"In commands, you is understood.","r":"we"},{"q":"8. “Are we expected to do homework every day?” Main verb / verb phrase?","o":["every","homework","are expected (to do)"],"a":2,"h":"Find the verb.","r":"are expected (to do)"}]},{"i":"📐","n":"Check! 2 · Complete the rules","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 91, Check! Exercise 2. Word bank: passive · past · person · subject.","items":[{"q":"We form the present simple passive with be followed by the ___ participle.","o":["past","person","subject"],"a":0,"h":"V3.","r":"past"},{"q":"The object of the active sentence becomes the ___ in a passive sentence.","o":["past","subject","passive"],"a":1,"h":"It moves to the front.","r":"subject"},{"q":"We use the passive when the ___ who did the action isn’t known or isn’t important.","o":["past","passive","person"],"a":2,"h":"Who did it?","r":"person"},{"q":"We cannot use the ___ with intransitive verbs (verbs that don’t have an object).","o":["passive","subject","person"],"a":0,"h":"No object → no passive.","r":"passive"}]},{"i":"✏️","n":"Focus 1 · Present simple passive","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 91, Focus Exercise 1. Complete using the present simple passive of the verbs in brackets.","items":[{"q":"a. You ___ two hours of homework every day. (encourage, do)","o":["encourage to do","are encouraged to do","are encouraging to do"],"a":1,"h":"be + V3 + to + verb.","r":"are encouraged to do"},{"q":"b. They ___ a school uniform. (expect, wear)","o":["expect to wear","are expecting wear","are expected to wear"],"a":2,"h":"Passive.","r":"are expected to wear"},{"q":"c. We ___ our homework by email. (ask, send)","o":["are asked to send","are asking send","ask to send"],"a":0,"h":"Passive.","r":"are asked to send"},{"q":"d. I ___ four books every month. (expect, read)","o":["expect to read","am expected to read","am expecting read"],"a":1,"h":"I + am.","r":"am expected to read"},{"q":"e. How teenagers spend their time ___ important for brain development. (think, be)","o":["is thinking be","thinks to be","is thought to be"],"a":2,"h":"Singular subject.","r":"is thought to be"},{"q":"f. My brother ___ to use his mobile phone in class. (not allow)","o":["isn’t allowed","isn’t allow","doesn’t allow"],"a":0,"h":"Passive negative.","r":"isn’t allowed"}]},{"i":"🤔","n":"Practice 2 · be supposed to or I suppose?","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"be supposed to + V = expected / should happen. I suppose (that) … = I think / I guess.","items":[{"q":"a. We should go now — I’m ___ home by six o’clock.","o":["suppose to be","supposed to be","supposing to be"],"a":1,"h":"be supposed to.","r":"supposed to be"},{"q":"b. Be careful, ___ our phones in class.","o":["we not supposed to use","we don’t suppose to use","we’re not supposed to use"],"a":2,"h":"Passive negative.","r":"we’re not supposed to use"},{"q":"c. Do you want to borrow my book? ___ But I need it back by Friday.","o":["I suppose so","I’m supposed so","I’m suppose so"],"a":0,"h":"Opinion / agreement.","r":"I suppose so"},{"q":"d. You know the trip on Monday — ___ our own lunch?","o":["do we suppose to take","are we supposed to take","we are supposed take"],"a":1,"h":"Question with be.","r":"are we supposed to take"}]},{"i":"❓","n":"Challenge 3 · Ask about your school","t":"book","lbl":"Q&A","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":20,"h":"❓ Workbook Challenge Exercise 3. Use the words to make a passive question, then answer about your school. Write: question + your answer.","items":[["a","a","What kind of clothes / you / expect / wear","What kind of clothes are you expected to wear? — At my school, …",["are you expected to"],"are you expected to wear"],["b","b","students / ask / work in groups?","Are students asked to work in groups? — …",["Are students asked to"],"are students asked to work"],["c","c","doing projects / think / be / a good way to learn?","Is doing projects thought to be a good way to learn? — …",["thought to be"],"thought to be"],["d","d","you / expect / collaborate or compete?","Are you expected to collaborate or compete? — …",["Are you expected to"],"are you expected to collaborate"],["e","e","What books / you / encourage / read?","What books are you encouraged to read? — …",["are you encouraged to"],"are you encouraged to read"],["f","f","How many hours / you / expect / study / every day?","How many hours are you expected to study every day? — …",["are you expected to"],"are you expected to study"]]},{"i":"📝","n":"FINAL BOSS · School rules reporter","t":"final","px":10,"h":"📝 Write 4–6 sentences about the rules at your school. Use at least three structures: are expected to · are allowed to · are not allowed to · are encouraged to · are supposed to.","hint":"Students are expected to … We are not allowed to … We are encouraged to …","ph":"At my school, students are expected to … We are not allowed to … We are encouraged to …","checks":[["3+ passive + infinitive structures","(am|is|are|’re|’m|’s) (not )?(expected|allowed|encouraged|supposed|asked) to",3],["Uses am / is / are","\\b(am|is|are)\\b|’re|’m|’s",1],["Uses to + base verb after the passive","(expected|allowed|encouraged|supposed|asked) to [a-z]+",1],["Describes real rules at school","school|class|teacher|uniform|homework|phone|students",1],["Clear English (4–6 sentences)",".{100,}",1]],"sk":["I understand the present simple passive.","I can use passive verbs followed by to-infinitive.","I can distinguish be supposed to from I suppose.","I can form questions about school rules."]}],"mx":78};
MX["v5.0"]={"code":"USE OF ENGLISH","title":"The Conversation Detective","q":"Reported questions and statements · DECODE → CHECK! → TENSE CHART → ORIGINAL WORDS → REPORTING VERBS → JASON’S CONVERSATION","end":{"t":"🕵️ THE CONVERSATION DETECTIVE – COMPLETE","did":"You decoded reported speech, sorted reported statements, questions and commands, completed the tense chart, recovered original words and reported Jason’s conversation. ✓ Tense and pronoun changes · ✓ Reported questions · ✓ tell / ask + object + to-infinitive.","r":"After this lab, I can …"},"steps":[{"i":"🧬","n":"Grammar decoder","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Direct: Fatima said, “I am busy.” Reported: Fatima said (that) she was busy. Questions: if / whether (Yes/No) or question word + subject + verb. Commands: tell / ask + object + (not) to + V1.","items":[{"q":"“I live here.” →","o":["She said she lives here.","She said she lived there.","She said me she lived there."],"a":1,"h":"Present simple → past simple; here → there.","r":"She said she lived there."},{"q":"“Are you busy?” →","o":["She asked that I was busy.","She asked if was I busy.","She asked if I was busy."],"a":2,"h":"Statement order.","r":"She asked if I was busy."},{"q":"“Where do you live?” →","o":["He asked where I lived.","He asked where I live do.","He asked where did I live."],"a":0,"h":"No inversion.","r":"He asked where I lived."},{"q":"“Don’t be late.” →","o":["She told not me to be late.","She told me not to be late.","She said me don’t be late."],"a":1,"h":"tell + object + not to.","r":"She told me not to be late."}]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Check! 1 · Identify the reported speech","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 93, Check! Exercise 1. Numbered parts: 1. She said she’d be here at 4 p.m. · 2. She asked me to wait for her at the school gate · 3. [She] told me not to be late · 4. Fatima told me that she had to stay late after class today · 5. She asked me if I was going to see you. (In the book, the example for a is [1].)","items":[{"q":"a. Two reported statements.","o":["3 and 5","2 and 3","1 and 4"],"a":2,"h":"said / told + that-clause.","r":"1 and 4"},{"q":"b. Two reported questions (the two ‘asked’ examples).","o":["2 and 5","3 and 4","1 and 4"],"a":0,"h":"5 is a yes/no question; 2 is a request with ask + infinitive.","r":"2 and 5"},{"q":"c. A reported command.","o":["5","4","3"],"a":2,"h":"told me not to be late.","r":"3"}]},{"i":"📊","n":"Check! 2 · Tense chart","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 93, Check! Exercise 2. Complete the chart: direct → reported.","items":[{"q":"1. Present simple →","o":["present perfect","past simple","would"],"a":1,"h":"Back one step.","r":"past simple"},{"q":"2. Present continuous →","o":["present continuous","past perfect","past continuous"],"a":2,"h":"was/were + -ing.","r":"past continuous"},{"q":"3. Present perfect →","o":["past perfect","past simple","would have"],"a":0,"h":"had + V3.","r":"past perfect"},{"q":"4. will →","o":["will","would","could"],"a":1,"h":"Modal.","r":"would"},{"q":"5. can →","o":["would","can","could"],"a":2,"h":"Modal.","r":"could"}]},{"i":"🔁","n":"Focus 1 · Recover the original words","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 94, Focus Exercise 1. Write the original words that were spoken.","items":[{"q":"a. She said she’d meet me at 4 p.m. → ‘I ___ at 4 p.m.’","o":["will meet you","meeting you","met you"],"a":0,"h":"would → will.","r":"I’ll meet you"},{"q":"b. She asked me to wait for her at the school gate. → ‘Please ___ at the school gate.’","o":["waiting for me","wait for me","waited for her"],"a":1,"h":"Imperative.","r":"wait for me"},{"q":"c. She told me not to be late. → ‘Please ___ late.’","o":["aren’t be","not be","don’t be"],"a":2,"h":"Negative imperative.","r":"don’t be"},{"q":"d. She told me that she had to stay late after class today. → ‘I ___ stay late after class today.’","o":["have to","will have","had to"],"a":0,"h":"Past → present.","r":"have to"},{"q":"e. She asked me if I was going to see Salma. → ‘___ to see Salma?’","o":["Were you going","Are you going","Do you go"],"a":1,"h":"Question order.","r":"Are you going"}]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"Practice 2 · Reporting verbs","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 94, Practice Exercise 2. Choose the best reporting option.","items":[{"q":"a. The article ___ that the family had followed a different schedule.","o":["mentioned","wrote"],"a":0,"h":"mention (that) + clause.","r":"mentioned"},{"q":"b. In his email, he ___ that he had already booked a place to stay.","o":["told","said"],"a":1,"h":"told needs a person.","r":"said"},{"q":"c. In the directions, it ___ where we could park.","o":["didn’t say","wasn’t said"],"a":0,"h":"Active sentence.","r":"didn’t say"},{"q":"d. I loved it, but my parents ___ that it was too expensive.","o":["told","said"],"a":1,"h":"No person after.","r":"said"},{"q":"e. The advert ___ how much the tickets were.","o":["didn’t mention","didn’t tell"],"a":0,"h":"mention.","r":"didn’t mention"},{"q":"f. Adam ___ me to help him get the food ready.","o":["requested","asked"],"a":1,"h":"ask + person + to.","r":"asked"}]},{"i":"✅","n":"Get it right! · say / tell / ask","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"say (that) + clause · tell + person + (that) + clause · ask + person + if / wh- + clause · ask + person + to-infinitive · mention (that) + clause.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["She said me she was busy.","She told she was busy.","She told me she was busy."],"a":2,"h":"tell + person.","r":"She told me she was busy."},{"q":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["He asked where I was.","He asked where am I.","He asked where was I."],"a":0,"h":"Statement order.","r":"He asked where I was."},{"q":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["He asked me helping him.","He asked me to help him.","He asked me help him."],"a":1,"h":"ask + person + to + V.","r":"He asked me to help him."}]},{"i":"🧪","n":"Compare with a model","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Key sentences from Jason’s conversation. (Model sentences are AI-made from the Workbook conversation, not the official key.)","items":[{"q":"Jason: “Can I go over to my friend’s house after school?” →","o":["Jason asked his mother could he go over to his friend’s house after school.","Jason said his mother if he can go over to his friend’s house.","Jason asked his mother if he could go over to his friend’s house after school."],"a":2,"h":"if + could.","r":"Jason asked his mother if he could go over to his friend’s house after school."},{"q":"His mother: “Who do you want to visit?” →","o":["She asked who he wanted to visit.","She asked who did he want to visit.","She asked who do he want to visit."],"a":0,"h":"Statement order.","r":"His mother asked who he wanted to visit."},{"q":"His mother: “Don’t be any later than 7 p.m.” →","o":["She said him don’t be later than 7 p.m.","She told him not to be any later than 7 p.m.","She asked him if not be later."],"a":1,"h":"tell + object + not to.","r":"His mother told him not to be any later than 7 p.m."}]},{"i":"📝","n":"Challenge 3 · Report Jason’s conversation","t":"final","px":10,"h":"📝 Challenge Exercise 3. Rewrite the conversation in reported speech. Jason: “Can I go over to my friend’s house after school?” Mother: “Who do you want to visit?” Jason: “I want to go over to Luke’s. We’re doing a school project together.” Mother: “OK, that’s fine, but please phone me when you get there.” Jason: “Thanks, Mum! How long can I stay?” Mother: “Don’t be any later than 7 p.m.”","hint":"Jason asked his mother if … She asked who … Jason said that … She asked him to … Jason asked how long … She told him not to …","ph":"Jason asked his mother if he could go over to his friend’s house after school. She asked …","checks":[["Yes/No question with if or whether","asked (his mother |her |him )?(if|whether)",1],["Wh-question in statement word order","asked .*(who|how long) (he|she|they|jason)",2],["Request or command with ask/tell + object + to","(asked|told) (him|her|his mother|jason) (not )?to ",1],["Changes pronouns and tenses","he could|she could|he wanted|they were doing|she said|he said",2],["Complete report",".{200,}",1]],"sk":["I can identify reported statements, questions and commands.","I understand the common tense changes in reported speech.","I can report questions using the correct word order.","I can report requests and commands using ask/tell + object + infinitive."]}],"mx":59};
MX["w5.3"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.4","title":"The Right Thing Investigator","q":"What would you have done? · WARM-UP → THREE CASE FILES → GRAMMAR BOOSTER → FINAL CHALLENGE","end":{"t":"⚖️ THE RIGHT THING INVESTIGATOR – COMPLETE","did":"You read three difficult situations, answered the four Workbook questions for each, practised the third conditional and if only, and wrote a strong answer with an opinion, an alternative and a reason. ✓ Opinions · ✓ Reasons · ✓ Third conditional.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.5 – Rights and responsibilities."},"steps":[{"i":"🤔","n":"Warm-up · What would you do?","t":"think","x":3,"h":"🤔 You are in a hurry and see someone in trouble, but you are not sure how to help. What would you do?","lab":["🛑 STOP AND HELP","📣 TELL SOMEONE RESPONSIBLE","🚶 CARRY ON","💭 SOMETHING ELSE"],"items":[["Choose one.",[0,1,2,3],"choice"]],"pr":"Why did you choose that? Give one reason.","bt":"Lock my answer","sg":"Locked! Now read the three case files in your Workbook."},{"i":"🚗","n":"Case A · Magda and the locked car","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Workbook p. 95, Exercise 1. Magda saw a man trying to get into a car. She was late for her violin lesson and didn’t stop. She told her dad, who went to help. Read the full text in your book.","items":[{"q":"Why didn’t Magda stop to help?","o":["She didn’t think the man needed help.","She was late for her violin lesson and didn’t know what she could do.","She was afraid of the man."],"a":1,"h":"Check the text.","r":"She was late and didn’t know what she could do."}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Case A · Your answers","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":10,"h":"✍️ Case A. Answer the four Workbook questions. There is no single correct answer.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Would you have done the same?","Yes, I would have … / No, I would have …",["I would have done the same","I would have done something different","I’m not sure"],"would have|not sure"],["2️⃣","2","If not, what would you have done?","I would have …",["I would have"],"would have|n.a|same"],["3️⃣","3","What wouldn’t you have done?","I wouldn’t have …",["I wouldn’t have"],"wouldn.t have|n.a"],["4️⃣","4","Give reasons for your answers.","I think this because …",["because","so that"],"because|so that|since"]]},{"i":"🏠","n":"Case B · Jamal and the stranger","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Workbook p. 95. Jamal saw a man climb into the back garden of a house. His bus arrived and he got on without doing anything. Read the full text in your book.","items":[{"q":"What would be the most sensible response? (suggested answer)","o":["Ignore the situation completely.","Confront the stranger alone.","Tell a trusted adult or the appropriate authorities."],"a":2,"h":"Think about safety.","r":"Tell a trusted adult or the authorities."}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Case B · Your answers","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":10,"h":"✍️ Case B. Answer the four Workbook questions.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Would you have done the same?","Yes, I would have … / No, I would have …",["I would have done the same","I would have done something different","I’m not sure"],"would have|not sure"],["2️⃣","2","If not, what would you have done?","I would have …",["I would have"],"would have|n.a|same"],["3️⃣","3","What wouldn’t you have done?","I wouldn’t have …",["I wouldn’t have"],"wouldn.t have|n.a"],["4️⃣","4","Give reasons for your answers.","I think this because …",["because","so that"],"because|so that|since"]]},{"i":"🎒","n":"Case C · Reza and the younger boy","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Workbook p. 95. Reza saw three boys making fun of a younger boy and passing his bag around. He phoned the school office. Read the full text in your book.","items":[{"q":"How did Reza respond?","o":["He phoned the school office to report what was happening.","He joined the boys.","He took the school bag and went home."],"a":0,"h":"Check the text.","r":"He phoned the school office."}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Case C · Your answers","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":10,"h":"✍️ Case C. Answer the four Workbook questions.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Would you have done the same?","Yes, I would have … / No, I would have …",["I would have done the same","I would have done something different","I’m not sure"],"would have|not sure"],["2️⃣","2","If not, what would you have done?","I would have …",["I would have"],"would have|n.a|same"],["3️⃣","3","What wouldn’t you have done?","I wouldn’t have …",["I wouldn’t have"],"wouldn.t have|n.a"],["4️⃣","4","Give reasons for your answers.","I think this because …",["because","so that"],"because|so that|since"]]},{"i":"🧪","n":"Grammar booster","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Third conditional: If + past perfect, would have + V3. If only + past perfect expresses regret.","items":[{"q":"If Reza ___ the incident, the teachers might not have known about it.","o":["wouldn’t report","hadn’t reported","didn’t report"],"a":1,"h":"If-clause: had + V3.","r":"hadn’t reported"},{"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["If only Magda would have stopped!","If only Magda stops!","If only Magda had stopped!"],"a":2,"h":"if only + had + V3.","r":"If only Magda had stopped!"},{"q":"If I had stopped, I ___ the man.","o":["would have helped","would help","had helped"],"a":0,"h":"Result clause.","r":"would have helped"}]},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL CHALLENGE · Stronger answer","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Choose the case you find most difficult (A, B or C). Write: Opinion (would you have done the same?), Alternative (what would you have done?) and Reason (why?).","hint":"In Case …, I would / wouldn’t have … because … If I had …, I would have …","ph":"In Case … I would have … because … If I had …, I would have …","checks":[["Chooses a case","case|magda|jamal|reza",1],["Opinion","would have|wouldn.t have|same|different",1],["Alternative action","instead|would have|rather|different",1],["Reason","because|so that|since",1],["Uses third conditional","if .*had [a-z]+.*would have",1]],"sk":["I read and understood all three situations.","I answered the four questions for each situation.","I can use the third conditional to talk about an imagined past result.","I explained my opinion with specific reasons."]}],"mx":79};
MX["w5.4"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.5","title":"Becoming a Responsible Citizen","q":"What do rights and responsibilities look like in adult life? · WARM-UP → FIVE TEXTS → VOCABULARY → MY OPINION","end":{"t":"🗳️ RESPONSIBLE CITIZEN – COMPLETE","did":"You completed five texts about adult responsibilities, matched key expressions and explained which two actions you would (or wouldn’t) do in the future. ✓ Citizenship vocabulary · ✓ Opinions with reasons.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.6 – What happened?"},"steps":[{"i":"🌱","n":"Warm-up · Growing up","t":"think","x":3,"h":"🌱 Which responsibility would you most like to take on when you become an adult?","lab":["💼 FIRST JOB","🏦 BANK ACCOUNT","🗳️ VOTING","🤝 HELPING PEOPLE"],"items":[["Choose one.",[0,1,2,3],"choice"]],"pr":"Why? Give one reason.","bt":"Lock my answer","sg":"Locked! Now complete the texts in your Workbook."},{"i":"💼","n":"Ex 1 · Text A and B","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 96, Exercise 1. Word bank: a bank account · blood · do · full-time · give · home · joined · jury duty · learned · left · open · part-time · the army · to drive · to vote · was working · donate. Text A: “The first thing I did when I got my first job was to (1). I was only 15 and I only had a (2) job at the local newsagent on Saturdays…” Text B: “I (3) when I was 17 because I wanted to learn a trade… I (4) a lorry and got good training as a mechanic.”","items":[{"q":"Gap 1: The first thing I did when I got my first job was to ___.","o":["join the army","open a bank account","learned to drive"],"a":1,"h":"Keeping track of earnings.","r":"open a bank account"},{"q":"Gap 2: I only had a ___ job at the local newsagent on Saturdays.","o":["jury duty","full-time","part-time"],"a":2,"h":"Only Saturdays.","r":"part-time"},{"q":"Gap 3: I ___ when I was 17 because I wanted to learn a trade.","o":["joined the army","left home","gave blood"],"a":0,"h":"Training and career.","r":"joined the army"},{"q":"Gap 4: I ___ a lorry and got good training as a mechanic.","o":["was working","learned to drive","voted"],"a":1,"h":"learn to drive a lorry.","r":"learned to drive"}]},{"i":"🏠","n":"Ex 1 · Text C and D","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Text C: “I was really happy when I was old enough (6) in the general election… I (5) when I was 18 and went off to university.” Text D: “I was called up to (7) last year. I (8), so I had to get permission to take time off work…”","items":[{"q":"Gap 5: I ___ when I was 18 and went off to university.","o":["gave blood","joined the army","left home"],"a":2,"h":"Independence.","r":"left home"},{"q":"Gap 6: …old enough ___ in the general election.","o":["to vote","to drive","jury duty"],"a":0,"h":"Election.","r":"to vote"},{"q":"Gap 7: I was called up to ___ last year.","o":["give blood","do jury duty","open a bank account"],"a":1,"h":"A court case.","r":"do jury duty"},{"q":"Gap 8: I ___, so I had to get permission to take time off work.","o":["left home","was voting","was working full-time"],"a":2,"h":"Needed permission from work.","r":"was working full-time"}]},{"i":"🩸","n":"Ex 1 · Text E","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Text E: “There are several reasons to (9). Firstly, you can help people who are sick or have been in an accident…” Note: “donate” is also in the word bank.","items":[{"q":"Gap 9: There are several reasons to ___ blood.","o":["give","do","learn"],"a":0,"h":"give blood (donate blood also fits).","r":"give blood"}]},{"i":"📖","n":"Vocabulary booster","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Match the expression with its meaning.","items":[{"q":"open a bank account","o":["Công việc bán thời gian","Mở tài khoản ngân hàng","Học lái xe"],"a":1,"h":"Bank.","r":"Mở tài khoản ngân hàng"},{"q":"part-time job","o":["Gia nhập quân đội","Hiến máu","Công việc bán thời gian"],"a":2,"h":"Not full-time.","r":"Công việc bán thời gian"},{"q":"join the army","o":["Gia nhập quân đội","Hiến máu","Mở tài khoản ngân hàng"],"a":0,"h":"Military.","r":"Gia nhập quân đội"},{"q":"learn to drive","o":["Hiến máu","Học lái xe","Gia nhập quân đội"],"a":1,"h":"Driving.","r":"Học lái xe"},{"q":"leave home","o":["Công việc bán thời gian","Mở tài khoản ngân hàng","Rời nhà để sống độc lập"],"a":2,"h":"Independence.","r":"Rời nhà để sống độc lập"},{"q":"vote in an election","o":["Bỏ phiếu trong một cuộc bầu cử","Mở tài khoản ngân hàng","Công việc bán thời gian"],"a":0,"h":"Election.","r":"Bỏ phiếu trong một cuộc bầu cử"},{"q":"do jury duty","o":["Mở tài khoản ngân hàng","Thực hiện nghĩa vụ bồi thẩm đoàn","Gia nhập quân đội"],"a":1,"h":"Court.","r":"Thực hiện nghĩa vụ bồi thẩm đoàn"},{"q":"give blood","o":["Công việc bán thời gian","Học lái xe","Hiến máu"],"a":2,"h":"Donate.","r":"Hiến máu"}]},{"i":"💭","n":"Ex 2 · Give your opinion","t":"book","lbl":"EX 2","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":25,"h":"💭 Ex 2. Choose two actions (open a bank account · join the army · learn to drive · leave home to study · vote · do jury duty · give blood) and explain why you will or won’t do them in the future.","items":[["1️⃣","1","Action 1","I’d like to … because … / I probably won’t … because …",["I’d like to","I think it’s important to","I probably won’t"],"because"],["2️⃣","2","Action 2","One advantage is that … / It would give me the opportunity to …",["One advantage is that","It would give me the opportunity to","I’m not sure whether I would"],"because|advantage|opportunity"]]},{"i":"🏆","n":"FINAL CHALLENGE · A responsible adult","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Write 5–7 sentences about the two actions you chose. Say what you plan to do in the future and give a reason for each.","hint":"As I grow older, there are several responsibilities I may take on. Two things I would like to do are … because …","ph":"As I grow older, there are several responsibilities I may take on. Two things I would like to do are …","checks":[["Mentions two actions","bank account|army|drive|home|vote|voting|jury|blood|job",2],["Future plan or intention","will|would|going to|want to|plan to|’d like|probably",1],["Reason for each choice","because|so that|since|one advantage|opportunity",2],["Useful opinion language","i think|i’m not sure|i probably|it’s important|advantage",1],["Complete paragraph",".{150,}",1]],"sk":["I completed the gaps in Exercise 1.","I understand expressions about work, voting and citizenship.","I chose two actions in Exercise 2.","I explained my reasons and wrote in English."]}],"mx":59};
MX["w5.5"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.6","title":"The Witness Report","q":"Can you describe a scene accurately? · WARM-UP → VOCABULARY → OBSERVE → CORRECT THE ACCOUNT → PAST TENSES → WITNESS STATEMENT","end":{"t":"🕵️ THE WITNESS REPORT – COMPLETE","did":"You practised describing appearance, clothing and actions, checked a witness account against the photo, corrected mistakes and wrote your own witness statement. ✓ Description vocabulary · ✓ Past continuous and past simple · ✓ Accurate reporting.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.7 – Improve your writing."},"steps":[{"i":"👁️","n":"Warm-up · Become a witness","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"A good witness notices specific details instead of saying general things.","items":[{"q":"“What did the person look like?” asks about …","o":["Appearance","Action","Clothing"],"a":0,"h":"Hair, height, glasses.","r":"Appearance"},{"q":"“What was the person wearing?” asks about …","o":["Action","Clothing","Appearance"],"a":1,"h":"Coat, scarf, hat.","r":"Clothing"},{"q":"“What was the person doing?” asks about …","o":["Appearance","Clothing","Action"],"a":2,"h":"Riding, standing, eating.","r":"Action"}]},{"i":"🧰","n":"Vocabulary toolkit","t":"bucket","x":1,"h":"🧰 Sort the words: appearance, clothing or action.","hint":"Think: how they look, what they wear, what they do.","lab":["👤 APPEARANCE","👕 CLOTHING","🏃 ACTION"],"items":[["dark hair",0,"Appearance."],["glasses",0,"Appearance."],["short hair",0,"Appearance."],["tall",0,"Appearance."],["a scarf",1,"Clothing."],["a helmet",1,"Clothing."],["boots",1,"Clothing."],["a jacket",1,"Clothing."],["riding a bike",2,"Action."],["pushing a stroller",2,"Action."],["standing",2,"Action."],["eating",2,"Action."]],"sg":"💡 Now look at the photo in your Workbook (p. 97) and describe the people."},{"i":"🔭","n":"Ex 1 · Observe the scene","t":"book","lbl":"OBSERVE","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"oc":1,"h":"🔭 Ex 1. Look carefully at the photo in your Workbook. Describe what you see.","items":[["👤","1","Describe a person’s appearance.","The woman has … hair and she is …",["dark hair","fair hair","short hair","glasses","tall"],""],["👕","2","Describe what a person is wearing.","He is wearing …",["a jacket","a coat","a scarf","a hat","a helmet","boots"],"wearing"],["🏃","3","Describe what a person is doing.","She is riding / standing / eating …",["riding a bike","standing","eating","pushing a stroller"],"ing"]]},{"i":"🔎","n":"Ex 2 · Check the weather and details","t":"book","lbl":"PHOTO","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":8,"oc":1,"h":"🔎 Ex 2 support. Cover nothing yet: look at the photo and compare it with three details from the account. Do not guess; check the photo.","items":[["🌦️","1","Weather: was it raining in the photo?","In the photo, …",[],""],["💇","2","The woman riding towards the witness: what is her hair like?","In the photo, her hair is …",["dark","fair","short","long"],""],["🧥","3","The same woman: what is she wearing?","In the photo, she is wearing …",["a scarf","a coat","a jacket","a top"],""]]},{"i":"✏️","n":"Ex 2 · Correct the account","t":"book","lbl":"FIX","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":8,"h":"✏️ Ex 2. Cover the photo with a sheet of paper and read the witness account in your Workbook. Underline the ten mistakes and correct them. Write each corrected sentence.","items":[["1","1","Correction 1","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["2","2","Correction 2","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["3","3","Correction 3","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["4","4","Correction 4","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["5","5","Correction 5","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["6","6","Correction 6","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["7","7","Correction 7","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["8","8","Correction 8","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["9","9","Correction 9","Original mistake → correct version",[],""],["10","10","Correction 10","Original mistake → correct version",[],""]]},{"i":"⏱️","n":"Grammar booster","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"Past continuous (was/were + -ing) describes actions in progress. Past simple tells completed events.","items":[{"q":"People ___ their shopping when I saw them.","o":["were doing","was doing","did doing"],"a":0,"h":"Plural subject.","r":"were doing"},{"q":"A cyclist ___ towards me.","o":["were riding","was riding","is riding"],"a":1,"h":"Singular subject.","r":"was riding"},{"q":"While I ___ through the street, I noticed the cyclists.","o":["am walking","walked","was walking"],"a":2,"h":"Action in progress.","r":"was walking"},{"q":"I ___ the pedestrian zone and saw a crowd.","o":["entered","was entering","enter"],"a":0,"h":"Completed event.","r":"entered"}]},{"i":"📝","n":"FINAL CHALLENGE · Witness statement","t":"final","px":10,"h":"📝 Imagine you are telling about a crowded scene you witnessed. Write 4–6 sentences: one sentence describing the scene, two about actions in progress, one about appearance or clothing, and one about something you saw.","hint":"It was … People were … A man was … He was wearing … Then I saw …","ph":"It was a crowded street. People were … A woman was … She was wearing … Then I saw …","checks":[["Describes the scene","crowded|busy|street|it was",1],["Past continuous (actions in progress)","(was|were) [a-z]+ing",2],["Appearance or clothing","wearing|hair|glasses|tall|short|scarf|coat|jacket|hat",1],["Past simple (what you saw)","\\b(saw|noticed|heard|walked|arrived|stopped|looked)\\b",1],["4–6 sentences",".{120,}",1]],"sk":["I practised vocabulary for appearance, clothing and actions.","I read the witness account carefully.","I tried to correct the ten mistakes by checking the original photo.","I practised the past continuous and wrote a short witness statement."]}],"mx":117};
MX["u5.1"]={"code":"USE OF ENGLISH","title":"Rewrite the Past","q":"Third conditional · DECODE → CHECK! → FOCUS 1 → FOCUS 2 → PRACTICE → CHALLENGE","end":{"t":"⏪ REWRITE THE PAST – COMPLETE","did":"You decoded the third conditional, completed the rules, answered yes/no questions, chose correct forms, corrected mistakes and rewrote five sentences. ✓ If + past perfect, would have + V3 · ✓ if only / I wish.","r":"After this lab, I can …"},"steps":[{"i":"🧬","n":"Grammar decoder","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"If + past perfect, would have + past participle. Example: If I hadn’t played football, I would’ve been on time for lessons. The clauses can change places: I wouldn’t have missed the bus if I had got up earlier.","items":[{"q":"1. If I ___ earlier, I would have caught the bus.","o":["would have got up","got up","had got up"],"a":2,"h":"If-clause: had + V3.","r":"had got up"},{"q":"2. I ___ the test if I had studied harder.","o":["would have passed","would passed","had passed"],"a":0,"h":"would have + V3.","r":"would have passed"},{"q":"3. Which sentence is correct?","o":["If she called, I would have answered yesterday.","If she had called, I would have answered.","If she would have called, I had answered."],"a":1,"h":"had + V3 / would have + V3.","r":"If she had called, I would have answered."}]},{"i":"📐","n":"Check! · Complete the rules","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 98, Check! Word box: imaginary · only · perfect · would.","items":[{"q":"(1) We use the third conditional to talk about ___ past situations.","o":["would","perfect","imaginary"],"a":2,"h":"They did not happen.","r":"imaginary"},{"q":"(2) In the if-clause we use the past ___ form of the verb.","o":["perfect","imaginary","only"],"a":0,"h":"had + V3.","r":"perfect"},{"q":"(3) In the main clause we use ___ + have + past participle.","o":["imaginary","would","only"],"a":1,"h":"would have + V3.","r":"would"},{"q":"(4) We can use the if-clause with if ___ or I wish to express regret.","o":["would","perfect","only"],"a":2,"h":"if only.","r":"only"}]},{"i":"⚽","n":"Focus 1 · Yes or no?","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 98, Focus Exercise 1. The boy says: “If only I hadn’t played football with my friend this morning. If I hadn’t played football, I would’ve been on time for lessons. And I wouldn’t have got this detention!”","items":[{"q":"a. Did the boy play football this morning?","o":["Yes","No"],"a":0,"h":"The third conditional negates reality.","r":"Yes"},{"q":"b. Was he on time for his lessons?","o":["Yes","No"],"a":1,"h":"He would have been on time.","r":"No"},{"q":"c. Did he get a detention?","o":["Yes","No"],"a":0,"h":"wouldn’t have got → he did.","r":"Yes"}]},{"i":"⭕","n":"Focus 2 · Circle the correct words (a–d)","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 98, Focus Exercise 2. Choose the pair that fits (first blank / second blank).","items":[{"q":"a. If I ___ studied more, I ___ passed the test.","o":["had / would have","would have / had","had / had"],"a":0,"h":"if-clause / main clause.","r":"had / would have"},{"q":"b. You ___ won the match if you ___ practised more.","o":["had / would have","would have / had","would have / would have"],"a":1,"h":"main clause first.","r":"would have / had"},{"q":"c. They ___ called the doctor if they ___ been worried.","o":["hadn’t / wouldn’t have","hadn’t / hadn’t","wouldn’t have / hadn’t"],"a":2,"h":"main clause first.","r":"wouldn’t have / hadn’t"},{"q":"d. If Marie ___ listened more carefully, she ___ chosen the right answer.","o":["had / would have","had / had","would have / had"],"a":0,"h":"if-clause first.","r":"had / would have"}]},{"i":"⭕","n":"Focus 2 · Circle the correct words (e–g)","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 98, Focus Exercise 2 (continued).","items":[{"q":"e. If we ___ checked our email, we ___ known about the clothing sale.","o":["wouldn’t have / hadn’t","hadn’t / wouldn’t have","hadn’t / hadn’t"],"a":1,"h":"negative if-clause, negative result.","r":"hadn’t / wouldn’t have"},{"q":"f. If only I ___ forgotten my house keys this morning!","o":["forgot … forgotten","had … forgot","had … forgotten"],"a":2,"h":"if only + had + V3.","r":"had … forgotten"},{"q":"g. I wish we ___ worn our warm coats. It’s freezing in here.","o":["had … worn","hadn’t … worn","wore … worn"],"a":0,"h":"I wish + had + V3.","r":"had … worn"}]},{"i":"🛠️","n":"Practice 3 · Correct two mistakes in each sentence","t":"book","lbl":"FIX","sv":"Save","x":4,"min":15,"h":"🛠️ Workbook p. 99, Practice Exercise 3. Rewrite each sentence with the two mistakes corrected.","items":[["A","A","We wouldn’t gone to the station if we had know about the rail strike.","Correct sentence…",[],"(?=.*wouldn.t have gone)(?=.*had known)"],["B","B","If I hadn’t in a hurry, I would had complained about the bill.","Correct sentence…",[],"(?=.*hadn.t been in a hurry)(?=.*would have complained)"],["C","C","If Jake had left his bike outside, it wouldn’t have damaged by the rain.","Correct sentence…",[],"(?=.*had left)(?=.*wouldn.t have been damaged)"],["D","D","If we had saw the lost cat, we would have report it to the owners.","Correct sentence…",[],"(?=.*had seen)(?=.*would have reported)"],["E","E","What you would have done if you had forgot your passport?","Correct sentence…",[],"(?=.*what would you have done)(?=.*had forgotten)"],["F","F","Would he have go to the dentist if he had break his tooth?","Correct sentence…",[],"(?=.*would he have gone)(?=.*had broken)"]]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Challenge 4 · Rewrite with the third conditional","t":"book","lbl":"REWRITE","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":20,"h":"✍️ Workbook p. 99, Challenge Exercise 4. Identify the real past event first, then make it an imagined condition.","items":[["A","A","He didn’t put money in the parking meter so he got a fine. → If he had …","If he had put money in the parking meter, …",[],"if he had put.*(wouldn.t have|would not have)"],["B","B","I had my phone with me, so I was able to call the emergency services. → If I hadn’t …","If I hadn’t had my phone with me, …",[],"if i hadn.t had.*(wouldn.t have|would not have)"],["C","C","I didn’t know you were in trouble, so I didn’t help you. → If I had …","If I had known you were in trouble, …",[],"if i had known.*would have"],["D","D","He passed the test, so he got his driving licence. → If he hadn’t …","If he hadn’t passed the test, …",[],"if he hadn.t passed.*(wouldn.t have|would not have)"],["E","E","You looked out of the window and so you saw the birds escaping. → If you hadn’t …","If you hadn’t looked out of the window, …",[],"if you hadn.t looked.*(wouldn.t have|would not have)"]],"sg":"💡 Model (AI-made, not official): A If he had put money in the meter, he wouldn’t have got a fine. B If I hadn’t had my phone, I wouldn’t have been able to call the emergency services. C If I had known you were in trouble, I would have helped you. D If he hadn’t passed the test, he wouldn’t have got his driving licence. E If you hadn’t looked out of the window, you wouldn’t have seen the birds escaping."},{"i":"💭","n":"Remember · If only / I wish","t":"final","px":10,"h":"💭 Write 4–5 sentences about a time you regret something. Use the third conditional twice, one sentence with “If only …” and one with “I wish …”.","hint":"If I had …, I would have … If only I had … I wish I had …","ph":"If I had studied more, I would have passed the test. If only I had …. I wish I had ….","checks":[["Third conditional (2 sentences)","if .*had [a-z]+.*(would|wouldn.t) have",2],["If only + past perfect","if only .*had [a-z]+",1],["I wish + past perfect","i wish .*had [a-z]+",1],["Complete sentences",".{120,}",1]],"sk":["I remember if + past perfect, would have + past participle.","I completed the Check! and Focus parts.","I corrected two mistakes in each Practice sentence.","I rewrote five sentences with the third conditional in the Challenge."]}],"mx":83};
MX["v5.1"]={"code":"USE OF ENGLISH","title":"Reconstruct the Moment","q":"Past continuous · DECODE → CHECK! → FOCUS 1 → FOCUS 2 → PRACTICE → CHALLENGE → MINI STORY","end":{"t":"🎬 RECONSTRUCT THE MOMENT – COMPLETE","did":"You decoded the past continuous, matched it to its uses, chose the right verb forms, corrected conversations and wrote a mini story with an interrupting event and a past intention. ✓ was/were + V-ing · ✓ interrupting past simple · ✓ was/were going to.","r":"After this lab, I can …"},"steps":[{"i":"🧬","n":"Grammar decoder","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"was/were + V-ing. Uses: (A) scene / background, (B) action in progress interrupted by another action (past continuous + past simple), (C) past intentions with was/were going to.","items":[{"q":"1. At 8 p.m. yesterday, I ___ my homework.","o":["was doing","did"],"a":0,"h":"Action in progress at a time.","r":"was doing"},{"q":"2. I ___ my homework when the lights went out.","o":["did","was doing"],"a":1,"h":"Interrupted action.","r":"was doing"},{"q":"3. We ___ to go swimming, but it started raining.","o":["were going","went"],"a":0,"h":"Past intention.","r":"were going"}]},{"i":"📐","n":"Check! · Complete the rules","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Workbook p. 100, Check! Word box: background · intentions · interrupts · progress · same · scene.","items":[{"q":"1. We use the past continuous to describe a ___ or to give ___ information.","o":["interrupts / intentions","progress / same","scene / background"],"a":2,"h":"Setting.","r":"scene / background"},{"q":"2. We often use the past continuous and the past simple in the ___ sentence.","o":["same","scene","progress"],"a":0,"h":"One sentence.","r":"same"},{"q":"3. We use the past continuous for an action in ___.","o":["interrupts","progress","intentions"],"a":1,"h":"Ongoing.","r":"progress"},{"q":"4. We use the past simple for an action which ___ it.","o":["background","same","interrupts"],"a":2,"h":"Cuts in.","r":"interrupts"},{"q":"5. We use the past continuous form of be going to for past ___.","o":["intentions","scene","progress"],"a":0,"h":"Plans.","r":"intentions"}]},{"i":"🚲","n":"Focus 1 · Match with the rules","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 100, Focus Exercise 1. Caption: a group of cyclists wearing helmets, not going fast, about to turn right when a large lorry drove past. a = scene / background · b = action in progress interrupted · c = past intention.","items":[{"q":"1. We were cycling along the main street.","o":["a","b","c"],"a":0,"h":"Sets the scene.","r":"a"},{"q":"2. We were all wearing helmets.","o":["b","a","c"],"a":1,"h":"Background.","r":"a"},{"q":"3. We weren’t going very fast.","o":["c","b","a"],"a":2,"h":"Background.","r":"a"},{"q":"4. We were going to turn right when suddenly a large lorry drove past us.","o":["a","c","b"],"a":1,"h":"was going to = past intention (it also has an interruption).","r":"c"}]},{"i":"⭕","n":"Focus 2 · Choose the verb forms (a–c)","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 100, Focus Exercise 2. Choose the best verb forms.","items":[{"q":"a. I ___ to school when suddenly I ___ a rabbit.","o":["was walking / was seeing","was walking / saw","walked / saw"],"a":1,"h":"Progress + interrupting event.","r":"was walking / saw"},{"q":"b. The cars ___ because some schoolchildren ___ the road.","o":["stopped / crossed","were stopping / crossed","stopped / were crossing"],"a":2,"h":"Completed + background.","r":"stopped / were crossing"},{"q":"c. It was a beautiful day; the sun ___ and the birds ___.","o":["was shining / were singing","shone / sang","was shining / sang"],"a":0,"h":"Scene.","r":"was shining / were singing"}]},{"i":"⭕","n":"Focus 2 · Choose the verb forms (d–f)","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 100, Focus Exercise 2 (continued). Item e: the extracted options are unclear, check your book.","items":[{"q":"d. As soon as the school bell ___, everyone ___ to the cafeteria.","o":["rang / was going to","rang / went","was ringing / was going"],"a":1,"h":"Two completed events.","r":"rang / went"},{"q":"e. We ___ to go to the park to play football, but it was too cold.","o":["were going to go","went"],"a":0,"h":"Past intention (the book’s options are went / were going to go).","r":"were going to go"},{"q":"f. They ___ at the bus stop, so the bus ___ past them.","o":["weren’t standing / drove","didn’t stand / was driving","weren’t standing / was driving"],"a":0,"h":"Background + event.","r":"weren’t standing / drove"}]},{"i":"💬","n":"Practice 3 · Past continuous in conversations","t":"book","lbl":"FIX","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"💬 Workbook p. 101, Practice Exercise 3. Read the conversations in your book. Rewrite the verbs that could be past continuous. Not every verb needs to change.","items":[["A","A","A: Did you go anywhere last weekend? B: It rained so we played computer games at home.","B: It was raining so we …",[],"was raining|were playing"],["B","B","A: Why didn’t you meet me after school yesterday? I waited for you. B: Sorry! I talked to the teacher about my project.","B: Sorry! I was …",[],"was talking|were talking"],["C","C","A: I saw you on the bus yesterday. Where did you go? B: I went to visit my grandma, but she phoned…","A: Where were you going? B: I was going to visit my grandma, but …",[],"were you going|was going"],["D","D","A: I rode my bike yesterday when I ran into a tree. B: Oh no! What did you do?","A: I was riding my bike yesterday when I ran into a tree.",[],"was riding"]],"sg":"💡 Suggestions (AI-made, not official): A It was raining so we played computer games at home. B I was talking to the teacher about my project. C Where were you going? / I was going to visit my grandma, but she phoned … so I went shopping instead. D I was riding my bike yesterday when I ran into a tree."},{"i":"🧩","n":"Challenge 4 · A–C","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 101, Challenge Exercise 4. Write the verbs in the past continuous or the past simple.","items":[{"q":"A. He ___ (sit) under an apple tree when an apple ___ (fall) on his head.","o":["was sitting / was falling","was sitting / fell","sat / was falling"],"a":1,"h":"Progress + event.","r":"was sitting / fell"},{"q":"B. When she ___ (arrive) at the cafe, she was disappointed that her friends ___ (not wait) for her.","o":["was arriving / didn’t wait","arrived / didn’t wait","arrived / weren’t waiting"],"a":2,"h":"Event + background.","r":"arrived / weren’t waiting"},{"q":"C. While they ___ (play) football in the park, it ___ (start) to rain.","o":["were playing / started","played / was starting","were playing / was starting"],"a":0,"h":"While + progress.","r":"were playing / started"}]},{"i":"🧩","n":"Challenge 4 · D–F","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 101, Challenge Exercise 4 (continued). Item E has three verbs.","items":[{"q":"D. My parents ___ (live) in Japan when they ___ (meet).","o":["lived / were meeting","were living / met","were living / were meeting"],"a":1,"h":"Background + event.","r":"were living / met"},{"q":"E. What ___ (do) you ___ (say) when you ___ (win) the prize?","o":["were / saying / winning","did / said / win","did / say / won"],"a":2,"h":"Question with did; completed events.","r":"did … say … won"},{"q":"F. We ___ (go) to buy you some flowers but we ___ (not have) time.","o":["were going / didn’t have","were going / weren’t having","went / weren’t having"],"a":0,"h":"Past intention + simple past.","r":"were going / didn’t have"}]},{"i":"📖","n":"FINAL CHALLENGE · What was happening?","t":"final","px":10,"h":"📖 Write a mini story of 4–5 sentences about an unexpected event. Use at least two past continuous verbs, one past simple for the interrupting event and one was/were going to.","hint":"I was … when … We were going to … but …","ph":"I was walking home when … We were going to … but …","checks":[["2+ past continuous","(was|were) [a-z]+ing",2],["Past simple interrupting event","when .*(saw|heard|fell|started|ran|stopped|arrived|rang|went|came|crashed)|(saw|heard|fell|started|ran|stopped|arrived|rang|went|came|crashed)",1],["was/were going to","(was|were) going to",1],["4–5 sentences",".{110,}",1]],"sk":["I remember was/were + V-ing.","I can tell an action in progress from an interrupting action.","I understand was/were going to for past intentions.","I completed Focus, Practice and Challenge."]}],"mx":70};
MX["w5.6"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.7","title":"Classroom Rules Reporter","q":"Can you answer a pen-friend’s questions about your school? · MATCH → PLAN → LANGUAGE → WRITE","end":{"t":"✉️ CLASSROOM RULES REPORTER – COMPLETE","did":"You matched Jackie’s questions with five topics, planned your ideas, used rules language and wrote a clear, polite email reply. ✓ Topics · ✓ Rules language · ✓ Email layout.","r":"Next: Workbook 6.8 – Project challenge."},"steps":[{"i":"🧩","n":"Ex 1 · Match the questions with the topics","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 102, Exercise 1. Read Jackie’s email in your book. Topics: Asking questions · Giving feedback · Break time · Group work · Technology.","items":[{"q":"1. phones, the internet","o":["Giving feedback","Break time","Technology","Asking questions","Group work"],"a":2,"h":"Which topic does the question ask about?","r":"Technology"},{"q":"2. stay in the classroom, go outside","o":["Giving feedback","Technology","Group work","Break time","Asking questions"],"a":3,"h":"Which topic does the question ask about?","r":"Break time"},{"q":"3. in groups or individually","o":["Break time","Technology","Asking questions","Giving feedback","Group work"],"a":4,"h":"Which topic does the question ask about?","r":"Group work"},{"q":"4. if you don’t understand something","o":["Asking questions","Technology","Break time","Group work","Giving feedback"],"a":0,"h":"Which topic does the question ask about?","r":"Asking questions"},{"q":"5. comments on your presentation","o":["Asking questions","Giving feedback","Technology","Break time","Group work"],"a":1,"h":"Which topic does the question ask about?","r":"Giving feedback"}]},{"i":"🧠","n":"Plan your ideas","t":"book","lbl":"TOPIC","sv":"Save","x":3,"min":10,"h":"🧠 Ex 2 planning. Jackie asks about five topics. Write notes about your school. You can answer all the questions or choose some.","items":[["📱","1","Technology: phones and the internet","We are allowed / aren’t allowed to …",["are allowed to","aren’t allowed to"],"allowed"],["⏰","2","Break time","During break time, we …",["stay in the classroom","go outside"],""],["👥","3","Group work","We are encouraged to work … / We usually work …",["are encouraged to"],""],["🙋","4","Asking questions","If we don’t understand something, we …",["have to","can"],""],["🎤","5","Giving feedback","When students give presentations, …",["comment on","suggest"],""]]},{"i":"🗣️","n":"Useful language","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Language for rules: We are allowed to… · We aren’t allowed to… · We have to… · We are encouraged to… · We are expected to… · I think these rules are…","items":[{"q":"Which expression says something is forbidden?","o":["We aren’t allowed to …","We have to …","We are encouraged to …"],"a":0,"h":"Not allowed.","r":"We aren’t allowed to …"},{"q":"Which expression says something is compulsory?","o":["We are allowed to …","We have to …","We are encouraged to …"],"a":1,"h":"Must do.","r":"We have to …"},{"q":"Which expression gives your opinion?","o":["We are expected to …","We are allowed to …","I think these rules are … because …"],"a":2,"h":"Opinion.","r":"I think these rules are … because …"}]},{"i":"✉️","n":"Ex 2 · FINAL · Reply to Jackie","t":"final","px":10,"h":"✉️ Ex 2. Reply to Jackie’s email by answering her questions about rules at your school. Start with Dear Jackie, and end politely. Use rules language: are allowed to · have to · are encouraged to · are expected to.","hint":"Dear Jackie, Thank you for your email. I’m happy to tell you about … We are allowed to … I think these rules are … because … I hope this information is helpful. Best wishes,","ph":"Dear Jackie,\n\nThank you for your email. I’m happy to tell you about the rules at my school.\n\n…\n\nBest wishes,","checks":[["Greeting and thanks","dear jackie|thank you|happy to tell",2],["Rules language (2+ structures)","(allowed to|have to|encouraged to|expected to|supposed to)",2],["Answers topics (technology, break, groups, questions, feedback)","phone|internet|break|group|individual|ask|presentation|feedback",3],["Gives an opinion with a reason","(i think|in my opinion).*because|because",1],["Polite ending","i hope|look forward|best wishes|helpful",1]],"sk":["I answered the questions I chose.","I used expressions such as are allowed to, have to or are encouraged to.","I organised my ideas into paragraphs.","I used a suitable greeting and ending.","I checked spelling, punctuation and verb forms."]}],"mx":41};
MX["w5.7"]={"code":"WORKBOOK 6.8","title":"Survive the Island!","q":"Can you survive and write about it? · COMPARE → IMAGINE → SURVIVAL RULES → DIARY","end":{"t":"🏝️ SURVIVE THE ISLAND! – COMPLETE","did":"You compared Robinson Crusoe and Alexander Selkirk, imagined island life, made survival rules and wrote a diary entry. ✓ Comparing texts · ✓ Giving opinions · ✓ Diary writing.","r":"Next: Unit 6 review."},"steps":[{"i":"📚","n":"Meet the two castaways","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Workbook p. 103, Exercise 1. Read the information about Robinson Crusoe (fictional character, novel by Daniel Defoe, 1719) and Alexander Selkirk (real Scottish sailor, 1704).","items":[{"q":"Which story is a work of fiction?","o":["Alexander Selkirk","Robinson Crusoe"],"a":1,"h":"Defoe’s novel.","r":"Robinson Crusoe"},{"q":"Who lived alone on an island for four years?","o":["Alexander Selkirk","Robinson Crusoe"],"a":0,"h":"The real sailor.","r":"Alexander Selkirk"},{"q":"Why was Alexander Selkirk left on the island?","o":["His ship was destroyed in a storm.","He refused to continue the journey."],"a":1,"h":"He was worried about the ship.","r":"He refused to continue the journey."},{"q":"How long was Robinson Crusoe stranded on the island?","o":["28 years","Four years"],"a":0,"h":"Check the text.","r":"28 years"}]},{"i":"⚖️","n":"Ex 1 · Same and different","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":25,"h":"⚖️ Ex 1. What are the similarities and differences between the two stories? Write notes first, then full sentences.","items":[["🟰","a","What is the same?","Both men … and they were both …",["both","also","similarly"],"both|same|similar"],["↔️","b","What is different?","Robinson Crusoe is …, whereas Alexander Selkirk was …",["whereas","however","but"],"whereas|however|but|different|while"]]},{"i":"💭","n":"Ex 2A · Like or dislike?","t":"book","lbl":"EX 2","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":20,"h":"💭 Ex 2. What do you think it would be like to be alone on a desert island for four years? What would you like or dislike about it?","items":[["😊","1","What would you like?","I would enjoy … because …",["peace and quiet","explore nature","become independent","have time to think"],"would|enjoy|like"],["😟","2","What would you dislike?","I would hate … because …",["feel lonely","no internet or phone","worry about food and water","miss my family"],"would|dislike|hate|miss"]]},{"i":"🛟","n":"Ex 2B · Survival rules","t":"book","lbl":"RULES","sv":"Save","x":6,"min":20,"h":"🛟 What kind of rules would you have to make in order to (i) keep fit and healthy, (ii) stay positive, (iii) send signals for help?","items":[["💪","i","Keep fit and healthy","To stay healthy, I would …",["find clean water","eat safe food","exercise every day"],"would|have to|must"],["🌈","ii","Stay positive","To stay positive, I would …",["a daily routine","keep a diary","set small goals"],"would|have to|must"],["🔥","iii","Send signals for help","To ask for help, I would …",["make signals on the beach","use smoke","watch for ships"],"would|have to|must"]]},{"i":"📓","n":"Diary language","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Diary entry: date and opening · feelings · actions and survival plans · ending (tomorrow). Useful: I felt terrified / lonely / relieved · I found…, I decided to… · Tomorrow, I would…","items":[{"q":"Which sentence is best for describing feelings?","o":["The island has trees.","I felt terrified and helpless.","Tomorrow is Monday."],"a":1,"h":"Feelings.","r":"I felt terrified and helpless."},{"q":"Which sentence describes a plan?","o":["The sea was very calm.","I was born in England.","I decided that I would build a shelter before nightfall."],"a":2,"h":"Plans.","r":"I decided that I would build a shelter."},{"q":"Which is a suitable diary opening?","o":["Dear Diary, Today was my first day on the island…","To whom it may concern,","Best wishes,"],"a":0,"h":"Diary.","r":"Dear Diary, Today was my first day…"}]},{"i":"✍️","n":"Ex 3 · FINAL · Diary entry","t":"final","px":10,"h":"✍️ Ex 3. Imagine you are Robinson Crusoe in your first week as a castaway. Write a diary entry. Use your answers from Exercise 2: feelings, actions and survival plans, and an ending about tomorrow.","hint":"Dear Diary, Today was … I felt … I found … I decided to … I would … Tomorrow, I will …","ph":"Dear Diary,\n\nToday was my first day on the island. I felt …","checks":[["Diary opening","dear diary",1],["Describes feelings","felt|frightened|lonely|terrified|relieved|determined|hopeful|scared",1],["Past actions","found|discovered|decided|looked|made|built|searched|explored",1],["Survival rules or plans","would|planned to|rules|water|food|shelter|signal",2],["Ending about tomorrow","tomorrow|hope|next",1]],"sk":["I compared the similarities and differences between the two stories.","I described what I would like or dislike about island life.","I suggested rules for health, positive thinking and asking for help.","My diary describes feelings, actions and plans.","I checked my spelling, punctuation and verb forms."]}],"mx":66};
MX["5.8"]={"code":"06.9","title":"Humankind: Six Boys on Ata","q":"What does a true story of survival tell us about human nature? · BOOK → EXTRACT → VOCAB → VALUES → INTERVIEW","end":{"t":"🏝️ MISSION COMPLETE – HUMANKIND","did":"You read about Humankind, found how six boys survived, discussed rules and human nature and wrote about their homecoming. 🏅 Badge: SURVIVAL STORYTELLER","r":"The story shows that people can … because …"},"steps":[{"i":"📘","n":"Ex 1 · About the book","t":"mcq","x":3,"ctx":"EX 1 (page 138). Read about Humankind (Rutger Bregman).","items":[{"q":"a. What kind of book is it?","o":["A non-fiction book about human nature and real events","A novel","A cookbook"],"a":0,"h":"It uses recent and historical events.","r":"Non-fiction"},{"q":"b. What does it aim to do?","o":["Teach how to build boats","Disprove the idea that humans are essentially selfish","Show that humans are essentially selfish"],"a":1,"h":"People tend to co-operate in crisis.","r":"To disprove the idea that humans are essentially selfish"}]},{"i":"💭","n":"Was it a good idea?","t":"book","lbl":"EX 1c","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"💭 EX 1c. Six boys from Tonga took a fishing boat out to sea at night, fell asleep and drifted for eight days. Was the boys’ ‘adventure’ a good idea? Why / why not?","items":[["⛵","c","Was the adventure a good idea?","I think it was / wasn’t a good idea because …",["because","dangerous"],"because"]]},{"i":"🎬","n":"Ex 2 · Video: how did they survive?","t":"mcq","x":3,"tr":"5.8","ctx":"🎬 Thay cho Track 37. Xem video <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/shipwreck-deserted-island-south-pacific-survivors-60-minutes-2021-04-04/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline text-blue-600\">A real life Lord of the Flies</a> (CBS News – 60 Minutes, 13 phút 23 giây; Mano Totau, Sione Fataua, Peter Warner và Rutger Bregman kể lại). Video dài hơn bài nghe trong sách, nên có thể xem hai lượt: lượt 1 cho a–c, lượt 2 cho d–g. Bật phụ đề tiếng Anh nếu cần. How did the boys find ways to …?","items":[{"q":"a. get food","o":["They were fed every day by fishermen.","They had no food at all.","They ate raw fish they caught and eggs from seabird nests, and later grew bananas and beans in a garden."],"a":2,"h":"Early days: fish and eggs. Later: a garden.","r":"raw fish, eggs, then a garden of bananas and beans"},{"q":"b. deal with thirst (early on)","o":["In the re-enactment film, they quenched their thirst with seabirds’ eggs and blood.","They collected rainwater in bottles.","They drank from a river."],"a":0,"h":"Re-enactment film (‘The Castaways’).","r":"seabirds’ eggs and blood"},{"q":"c. cook and keep warm","o":["They never cooked their food.","They made a fire, cooked hot meals, and everyone had a duty to take care of the fire.","They used a lighter from the boat."],"a":1,"h":"Sione: ‘everybody have a duty for the fire’.","r":"a fire that everybody took care of, day and night"},{"q":"d. keep themselves fit and strong","o":["They ran around the island every morning.","They did no exercise.","They built a badminton court and a makeshift gym."],"a":2,"h":"They also built a hut and a garden.","r":"a badminton court and a makeshift gym"},{"q":"e. be organised","o":["They set up a roster, for example to keep a lookout for passing ships.","They had no plan at all.","One boy gave all the orders."],"a":0,"h":"Duties for the fire and the lookout.","r":"a roster of duties (fire, lookout)"},{"q":"f. find solutions to disagreements","o":["They asked the captain to decide.","They cooled off by walking to opposite sides of the island.","They stopped talking for a week."],"a":1,"h":"Mano: ‘We did, and we disagreed.’","r":"they walked to opposite sides of the island to cool off"},{"q":"g. keep themselves happy","o":["They played computer games.","They watched films.","They prayed together and made up a song while on the island."],"a":2,"h":"Sione prayed; they composed a song, ‘Siosionoa’.","r":"prayer and a song they composed"}]},{"i":"📖","n":"Vocabulary from the glossary","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Words from the glossary on pages 139–140.","items":[{"q":"memoirs","o":["memories that are written down","a type of boat","a list of jobs"],"a":0,"h":"Captain Warner wrote them.","r":"memories that are written down"},{"q":"roster","o":["a kind of fish","a list of names and the jobs each person has to do","a place to sleep"],"a":1,"h":"Garden, kitchen, guard duty.","r":"a list of jobs for each person"},{"q":"quarrel","o":["to cook food","to climb a cliff","to have a disagreement"],"a":2,"h":"Squabblers.","r":"to have a disagreement"},{"q":"makeshift","o":["simple and not well-made but fulfilling a need","brand new","very expensive"],"a":0,"h":"Kolo’s guitar.","r":"simple but does the job"},{"q":"lift (someone’s) spirits","o":["to build a raft","to make someone feel happier","to carry someone"],"a":1,"h":"Song and guitar.","r":"to make someone feel happier"},{"q":"jubilant","o":["very tired","very angry","very happy"],"a":2,"h":"When the boys returned.","r":"very happy"}]},{"i":"🧭","n":"Ex 3 · Values","t":"book","lbl":"EX 3","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":15,"h":"🧭 EX 3. Work in small groups, then write your ideas.","items":[["a","a","Why do you think the boys made rules?","I think the boys made rules because …",["to stay organised","to avoid fights","to survive"],"because"],["b","b","What does this real-life story tell you about human nature?","I think it shows that people …",["co-operate","help each other"],"people|humans|we"],["c","c","What do you think happened when the boys got back home to Tonga?","I think … (check the next page of your book)",[],""]]},{"i":"⛵","n":"The six boys’ story","t":"order","x":14,"items":[0],"h":"⛵ Put the story of the six boys in order.","hint":"From the boat to the rescue.","cards":["A. They drifted for eight days without food or water.","B. Captain Peter Warner found them and they were rescued.","C. They fell asleep and the boat drifted far from the shore.","D. They lived there for over a year with rules, a garden and a fire.","E. Six boys took a fishing boat from the harbour in Nuku’alofa.","F. They landed on the rocky, uninhabited island of Ata.","G. Warner hired the boys as the crew of his new boat, the Ata."],"ans":[4,2,0,5,3,1,6],"yl":"⛵ YOUR TIMELINE","ft":"⛵ TIMELINE SET","flow":["SET OUT","DRIFTING","EIGHT DAYS","LANDING","LIFE ON ATA","RESCUE","CREW"],"bm":"Not quite. They drift before they land, and they are rescued before Warner hires them."},{"i":"🤝","n":"Cooperation or problems?","t":"bucket","x":1,"h":"🤝⚠️ Sort the details from the extract.","hint":"Helping each other, or something that went wrong?","lab":["🤝 HOW THEY COOPERATED","⚠️ PROBLEMS THEY FACED"],"items":[["the raft fell apart in the surf",1],["kept the fire burning for more than a year",0],["hardly any rain all summer",1],["no food or water for eight days",1],["Stephen slipped and broke his leg",1],["a storm dropped a tree on their hut",1],["set Stephen’s leg using sticks and leaves",0],["imposed a time-out when they quarrelled",0],["worked in teams of two with a roster",0],["began and ended each day with song and prayer",0]],"sg":"💡 The story shows that people can cooperate even in a crisis."},{"i":"📝","n":"Ex 4 · Writing: the homecoming","t":"final","px":10,"h":"📝 EX 4. You are interviewing the boys for your newspaper. Describe their homecoming and include what they told you about their experiences. Begin: “When the six lost boys from Tonga returned home, there were scenes of great joy and happiness. I was able to ask them about their experiences of surviving on a deserted island. They told me that …”","hint":"When the six lost boys from Tonga returned home … They told me that they had … They said that …","ph":"When the six lost boys from Tonga returned home, there were scenes of great joy and happiness. I was able to ask them about their experiences of surviving on a deserted island. They told me that …","checks":[["Describes the homecoming","joy|happiness|jubilant|welcome|returned|island|Tonga",1],["Uses reported speech (told / said that)","(told me|said|told us) that",1],["Uses details from the story (food, water, fire, rules, guitar)","fire|garden|water|rain|roster|rules|guitar|leg|raft|storm|Ata|Warner",2],["Past perfect or past simple to report","(had|was|were|could|never) [a-z]+",1],["Complete paragraph",".{150,}",1]],"sk":["I can explain what Humankind is and what it aims to do.","I can find how the boys survived in the extract.","I can use new words from the glossary.","I can discuss why rules and co-operation matter.","I can write a newspaper-style account using reported speech."]}],"mx":93};
MX["5.9"]={"code":"U6","title":"Rules and Laws Master Check","q":"Can you use what you learned in Unit 6 – not just remember it? · RECALL → VOCABULARY → USE OF ENGLISH → CAN I DO IT?","end":{"t":"⚖️ RULES AND LAWS MASTER CHECK COMPLETE – UNIT 6","did":"You went through Unit 6: 🏫 school rules · 👨‍👩‍👧 family life · 🏠 house rules · ⚖️ moral dilemmas · 🗳️ rights and responsibilities · 🕵️ witnesses · ✉️ email · 🏝️ survival. SKILLS CHECKED: ✓ rules and behaviour vocabulary · ✓ passive + infinitive · ✓ reported speech · ✓ third conditional. 🏅 Badge: RULES AND LAWS MASTER – UNIT 6 COMPLETE.","r":"I can use English to talk about rules and laws – and I know what I still want to practise."},"steps":[{"i":"🧠","n":"Memory flash","t":"bucket","x":0,"h":"🧠 UNIT 6: RULES AND LAWS. For each topic, say aloud for 30 seconds: “What do I remember?” Then rate yourself.","hint":"","lab":["💪 a lot","🙂 some","🤔 not much"],"items":[["🏫 school rules",-1],["👨‍👩‍👧 family life and kaizen",-1],["🏠 house rules and reported speech",-1],["⚖️ moral dilemmas",-1],["🗳️ rights and responsibilities",-1],["🕵️ witness statements",-1],["🏝️ a true story of survival",-1]],"sg":"Great – now let’s see what you can really use."},{"i":"❓","n":"General knowledge quiz 1–5","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Check your progress, p. 141 (answers from Unit 6).","items":[{"q":"1. What are French school children not allowed to eat with their lunch? (Lesson 6.1, Ex 4)","o":["Tomato ketchup","Bread","Chocolate"],"a":0,"h":"Schools in France aren’t allowed to serve it.","r":"Tomato ketchup."},{"q":"2. Where is Stockholm?","o":["Spain","Sweden","Switzerland"],"a":1,"h":"The Swedish family in Lesson 6.2.","r":"Sweden (it is the capital)."},{"q":"3. Which language does the word kaizen come from and what does it mean?","o":["Chinese: family","Korean: speed","Japanese: improvement"],"a":2,"h":"Lesson 6.2.","r":"Japanese – ‘improvement’."},{"q":"4. In the UK, at what age can you open a bank account? (Lesson 6.5)","o":["13","16","18"],"a":0,"h":"The textbook list.","r":"13."},{"q":"5. What does it mean if you work ‘part-time’?","o":["You work fewer hours than a full working week.","You work only at night.","You work for free."],"a":0,"h":"Compare full-time.","r":"You work fewer hours than full-time."}]},{"i":"❓","n":"General knowledge quiz 6–10","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Check your progress, p. 141.","items":[{"q":"6. If you are asked to be part of a group who decide on a case in a court of law in the UK, you are going to do what?","o":["Part-time work","Jury service","Detention"],"a":1,"h":"Lesson 6.5.","r":"Jury service."},{"q":"7. What do you call a person who sees an event such as an accident and gives a formal statement?","o":["A cyclist","An executive","A witness"],"a":2,"h":"Lesson 6.6.","r":"A witness."},{"q":"8. On which form of transport would you find handlebars?","o":["A bicycle (or motorbike)","A bus","A train"],"a":0,"h":"Lesson 6.6.","r":"A bicycle."},{"q":"9. Why do cars and lorries have wing mirrors?","o":["To make the vehicle look nice","So the driver can see traffic beside and behind","To hold the doors"],"a":1,"h":"Lesson 6.6.","r":"To help the driver see around the vehicle."},{"q":"10. Someone who drives a car is a driver. What do you call someone who rides a bike?","o":["A walker","A pilot","A cyclist"],"a":2,"h":"Lesson 6.6.","r":"A cyclist."}]},{"i":"📖","n":"Vocabulary 1 · School text","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Words: behaviour · bullying · detention · respect · rules · strict · trouble. “Our school is quite (1). There are a lot of (2) and if you don’t follow them, you get into (3) and you sometimes get a (4), and have to stay behind after school. Good behaviour and (5) for other people are important. I think discipline is a good thing because it means there isn’t much bad (6), such as interruptions in lessons and (7) outside lessons.”","items":[{"q":"(1) Our school is quite ___.","o":["strict","bullying","respect"],"a":0,"h":"Adjective.","r":"strict"},{"q":"(2) There are a lot of ___ …","o":["trouble","rules","detention"],"a":1,"h":"Things you follow.","r":"rules"},{"q":"(3) …you get into ___ …","o":["detention","behaviour","trouble"],"a":2,"h":"get into trouble.","r":"trouble"},{"q":"(4) …you sometimes get a ___ …","o":["detention","rules","strict"],"a":0,"h":"get a detention.","r":"detention"},{"q":"(5) Good behaviour and ___ for other people…","o":["bullying","respect","trouble"],"a":1,"h":"respect for others.","r":"respect"},{"q":"(6) …there isn’t much bad ___ …","o":["detention","rules","behaviour"],"a":2,"h":"bad behaviour.","r":"behaviour"},{"q":"(7) …interruptions in lessons and ___ outside lessons.","o":["bullying","respect","strict"],"a":0,"h":"bad behaviour outside lessons.","r":"bullying"}]},{"i":"🛏️","n":"Vocabulary 2 · Verbs","t":"mcq","x":1,"ctx":"Verbs: ask · follow · give · get · leave · make · own.","items":[{"q":"a. It only takes a few seconds to ___ your bed, but I sometimes forget!","o":["own","make","ask"],"a":1,"h":"make your bed.","r":"make"},{"q":"b. I need to ___ permission to leave school early today.","o":["leave","give","ask"],"a":2,"h":"ask permission.","r":"ask"},{"q":"c. If you had ___ the rules, you wouldn’t have got into trouble.","o":["followed","asked","owned"],"a":0,"h":"Past participle.","r":"followed"},{"q":"d. How old do you have to be before you can ___ blood?","o":["get","give","follow"],"a":1,"h":"give blood.","r":"give"},{"q":"e. I don’t want to ___ home until I’ve finished my education.","o":["own","make","leave"],"a":2,"h":"leave home.","r":"leave"},{"q":"f. I’d like to ___ a house or a flat by the time I’m 30.","o":["own","follow","ask"],"a":0,"h":"own a house.","r":"own"},{"q":"g. My sister ___ married last week and we all went to the wedding.","o":["gave","got","left"],"a":1,"h":"Past of get.","r":"got"}]},{"i":"🔧","n":"Use of English 1 · Passive + infinitive","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Complete the sentences with the correct passive form of the verbs in brackets.","items":[{"q":"a. We have a list for household chores and everyone (expect) ___ to help out.","o":["expects","is expecting","is expected"],"a":2,"h":"Passive.","r":"is expected"},{"q":"b. We (not / allow) ___ to have our phones at the table. It’s a phone-free zone.","o":["aren’t allowed","don’t allow","not allowed"],"a":0,"h":"Passive negative.","r":"aren’t allowed"},{"q":"c. At school, we (encourage) ___ to learn to play a musical instrument, but it’s not compulsory.","o":["encourage","are encouraged","are encouraging"],"a":1,"h":"Passive.","r":"are encouraged"},{"q":"d. I (suppose) ___ to learn a poem for homework this evening but so far, I’ve only learned two lines.","o":["suppose","am supposing","am supposed"],"a":2,"h":"be supposed to.","r":"am supposed"}]},{"i":"💬","n":"Use of English 2 · Report the conversation","t":"book","lbl":"REPORT","sv":"Save","x":5,"min":12,"h":"💬 Report the conversation (the first two lines are examples in the book: Alina asked Carla to tell her about her school. Carla asked Alina what she wanted to know.) Report the next lines.","items":[["3️⃣","3","Alina: Are there a lot of rules?","Alina asked if / whether …",[],"asked (carla )?(if|whether) there (were|was) a lot of rules"],["4️⃣","4","Carla: We have a few, for example, we aren’t allowed to use mobile phones in the classroom.","Carla said (that) …",[],"(said|told).*(had a few|weren.t allowed|were not allowed)"],["5️⃣","5","Alina: That’s the same at my school.","Alina said (that) …",[],"(said|told|replied).*same"],["6️⃣","6","Carla: We have to wear a uniform.","Carla said (that) …",[],"(said|told).*(had to wear|have to wear)"],["7️⃣","7","Alina: Oh, we don’t, but we can’t wear jeans and things like that.","Alina said (that) …",[],"(said|told).*(didn.t|couldn.t wear|can.t wear)"],["8️⃣","8","Carla: I don’t mind wearing a uniform because you don’t have to think about what you’re going to put on in the morning!","Carla said (that) …",[],"(said|told).*(didn.t mind|did not mind)"]]},{"i":"⏪","n":"Use of English 3 · Third conditional","t":"mcq","x":2,"ctx":"Match the halves, using the correct form for the third conditional. Example: If you had put your clothes in the washing basket, I would have washed them for you.","items":[{"q":"If we (leave) earlier, …","o":["we wouldn’t have missed the school bus.","we would have missed the school bus.","we didn’t miss the school bus."],"a":0,"h":"If + had left, would have.","r":"If we had left earlier, we wouldn’t have missed the school bus."},{"q":"If you (not / arrive) late for class three times this week, …","o":["you hadn’t got a detention.","you wouldn’t have got a detention.","you would have got a detention."],"a":1,"h":"If you hadn’t arrived late…","r":"you wouldn’t have got a detention."},{"q":"If I (not / write) my essay so quickly, …","o":["I hadn’t made so many mistakes.","I would have made so many spelling mistakes.","I wouldn’t have made so many spelling mistakes."],"a":2,"h":"If I hadn’t written…","r":"I wouldn’t have made so many spelling mistakes."},{"q":"If they (read) the question more carefully, …","o":["they would have got the answer right.","they have got the answer right.","they got the answer right."],"a":0,"h":"If they had read…","r":"they would have got the answer right."}]},{"i":"🏆","n":"Can I do it? · Summary checklist","t":"final","px":10,"h":"🏆 Write 4–5 sentences about what you learned in Unit 6. Use at least one passive + infinitive sentence, one reported speech sentence and one third conditional sentence.","hint":"At school we are expected to … My friend told me that … If I had …, I would have …","ph":"At my school we are expected to … My friend told me that … If I had …, I would have …","checks":[["Passive + infinitive","(am|is|are|’re) (not )?(expected|allowed|encouraged|supposed|asked) to",1],["Reported speech","(said|told|asked) (me |us |him |her )?(that|if|whether|to)",1],["Third conditional","if .*had [a-z]+.*would have",1],["About rules, home or school","rule|school|home|law|permission|respect|behaviour",1],["Clear English (4–5 sentences)",".{110,}",1]],"sk":["I can talk about rules at school and at home, and report what other people said.","I can discuss moral dilemmas and say what I would have done in the same situation.","I can discuss rights and responsibilities.","I can identify inconsistencies in witness statements.","I can make a podcast about a moral dilemma.","I can read a true story about how making their own rules helped shipwrecked teenagers to survive."]}],"mx":80};

